/* 横向卡 · 第三科（分子生物学）第三张
   一个基因在这个细胞里转不转录 —— 两道关卡。

   出处是《现代分子生物学》第五版 §8.3 与 §8.4（印刷页 298–326），经
   20260828_molecure_lite/data/spine_ch8_transcription.js（18 步）和
   spine_ch8_epigenetics.js（18 步）转录。两份里 beyond 节点各 3 个和 1 个，
   卡上用到的都在书内，标了页码。

   ⚠ 为什么把这两份料合成一张卡，而不是各做一张。
   它们在回答**同一个问题**：这个基因在这个细胞里转不转录。
   只是答在两个不同的关卡上——
     关卡一「摸不摸得到」：染色质包得多紧、DNA 上有没有甲基。
     关卡二「摸到之后认不认得」：序列上有哪些元件、细胞手里有哪些蛋白。
   书自己把这条缝说破了（p.315）：甲基化让元件「缩进大沟里够不着」，
   **阻断恰好发生在蛋白质必须接触双螺旋的那一步**。
   两道关卡这个说法一旦立住，三十六个节点就都有位置可放。

   接卡 mb-int（酵母双杂交——它正建立在「两个结构域可以拆开」这件事上）、
   mb-ko（基因捕获里的「不带启动子的报告基因」）、12（启动子决定何时何地表达）、
   16（染色质、核小体）、pe-expr 与 pe-sys（启动子强度、报告基因）。

   ⚠ 图：《现代分子生物学》的扫描件不在这个仓库里，只有转录出来的文字。
   图 8-10 到 8-41 一张都没法裁，按 R4「要画的先记下不要画」，一张都没放。
   最该画的两张记在 LOGIC.md §16：启动子的两半（图 8-10）、CTD 磷酸化循环（p.301 手批）。 */

window.CARDS.push({
id:'mb-reg', cross:1, w:0,
q:'一个基因转不转录 —— 两道关卡',
qcn:'横向卡 · 第三科第三张 · 摸不摸得到（染色质与甲基化）· 认不认得出（顺式元件与反式因子）',
sub:'跨题共用 · 出处《现代分子生物学》第五版 §8.3 §8.4 · 接卡 mb-int、mb-ko、12、16、pe-expr',

cram:[
 {g:'开口 · 先把两道关卡说出来', gn:'这张卡有三十多个名字。<b>名字分两堆放，就不会串</b>：一堆管「蛋白摸不摸得到这段 DNA」，另一堆管「摸到之后认不认得」。'},

 {n:'01', t:'这是一件什么工作',
  ez:'“Transcriptional regulation asks one question. Will this gene be transcribed in this cell. Two kinds of thing decide it. Cis acting elements are D N A sequences carried by the gene itself. They encode no product. Trans acting factors are the proteins that bind those sequences. Only R N A polymerase two transcribes messenger R N A precursors. So regulating a protein coding gene comes down to one thing. What brings polymerase two to this promoter.”',
  ezcn:'<b>转录水平的调控回答一个问题：这个基因在这个细胞里会不会被转录。</b><b>决定它的东西分两类。</b><b>顺式作用元件是基因自身携带的 DNA 序列，它们本身不编码任何产物；反式作用因子是结合到这些序列上的蛋白质（还有一部分 RNA）。</b><b>而只有 RNA 聚合酶Ⅱ转录信使 RNA 前体——所以调控一个蛋白质编码基因，归根到底就是「什么东西把聚合酶Ⅱ引到这个启动子上」。</b>',
  big:'<b>顺式元件</b> ＝ 基因自己带的 DNA 序列（不编码产物）· <b>反式因子</b> ＝ 结合上去读它们的蛋白。<b>只有聚合酶Ⅱ转 mRNA 前体</b> → 调控 ＝ 什么把聚合酶Ⅱ引到这个启动子上',
  en:'“Transcriptional regulation in eukaryotes asks whether a given gene will be transcribed in a given cell, and two kinds of thing decide it. Cis-acting elements are DNA sequences the gene itself carries, such as promoters, enhancers and silencers. They encode no product. Trans-acting factors are the proteins, and some RNAs, that bind those elements. The third participant is RNA polymerase, of which eukaryotes have three, each transcribing different products. Only polymerase two transcribes messenger RNA precursors, so regulating a protein-coding gene comes down to one thing: what brings polymerase two to this gene’s promoter.”',
  note:'<b>「顺式 / 反式」这两个词的命名依据是「怎么起作用」，不是「在哪里」。</b>顺式 ＝ 作用在自己所在的那条 DNA 上；反式 ＝ 做出来的产物跑过去作用在别处。<span class="pg">p.298</span><br><b>最后那半句是整张卡的口令</b>：一切都在回答「什么把聚合酶Ⅱ引过来」。'},

 {n:'02', t:'脊梁 · 两道关卡',
  ez:'“All of it sorts into two gates. Gate one asks whether a protein can reach the double helix at all. Chromatin packing decides that. D N A methylation decides it too. Gate two asks whether the protein recognises what it reached. The sequence elements decide that. So does which factors the cell happens to own. The textbook joins them in one sentence. Methylation pulls the elements down into the major groove. Then the proteins cannot reach them.”',
  ezcn:'<b>三十多个名字分两道关卡放。</b><b>关卡一问的是：蛋白够不够得着这段双螺旋——由染色质包得多紧、DNA 上有没有甲基决定。</b><b>关卡二问的是：够着之后认不认得——由序列上有哪些元件、这个细胞手里恰好有哪些因子决定。</b><b>书自己把两者接在了一句话里：甲基化把元件缩进大沟里，蛋白就够不着了。</b>',
  big:'<b>关卡一 · 摸不摸得到</b>：染色质松不松 · 有没有甲基<br><b>关卡二 · 认不认得出</b>：有哪些元件 · 有哪些因子',
  en:'“Everything here sorts into two gates, and that is the easiest way to hold it. The first gate asks whether a protein can reach the double helix at all, and that is set by how tightly the chromatin is packed and by whether the DNA carries methyl groups. The second gate asks whether the protein recognises what it has reached, and that is set by which sequence elements are there and which factors the cell happens to own. The textbook joins the two in one sentence: methylation pulls the binding elements down into the major groove so the proteins can no longer reach them. The block falls exactly at the step where a protein has to touch the double helix.”',
  note:'<b>说完这一句就停。</b>这是八分答案的形状。他挑哪一道关卡，你讲哪一道——<b>不要一口气把两边都铺开</b>，铺开就是三十个名字，谁也记不住。'},

 {g:'关卡二 · 序列这一侧：顺式元件', gn:'先讲这一侧，因为它是他最可能问的。<b>四个元件：启动子 · 增强子 · 沉默子 · 绝缘子。</b>'},

 {n:'03', t:'启动子的两半 · 「从哪里起始」和「起始得多频繁」是两段不同的 DNA',
  ez:'“A eukaryotic promoter is a group of independent D N A sequences. They lie between the start site and about two hundred base pairs upstream. The start site is numbered plus one. Each element is seven to twenty base pairs long. The promoter splits into two halves. The core promoter is the minimum needed for normal initiation. It holds the start site and the TATA box. The TATA box sits twenty five to thirty base pairs upstream. Alone the core promoter only fixes where transcription starts. It gives a basal level and no more.”',
  ezcn:'<b>真核基因的启动子，是位于转录起始位点（+1）及其 5′ 上游 100～200 bp 以内的一组具有独立功能的 DNA 序列，每个元件长 7～20 bp。</b><b>它分成两半。</b><b>核心启动子是保证聚合酶Ⅱ正常起始转录所必需的最少序列，包括起始位点本身和位于 −25～−30 bp 的 TATA 盒。</b><b>⚠ 核心启动子单独起作用时，只能确定「从哪里起始」并产生基础水平的转录——「从哪里」和「多频繁」，是由两段不同的 DNA 分别决定的。</b>',
  big:'<b>核心启动子</b>（起始位点 ＋ <b>TATA 盒 −25～−30</b>）定<b>从哪里起始</b>，只给基础水平<br><b>上游启动子元件 UPE</b>（<b>CAAT 盒 CCAAT，约 −70</b> · <b>GC 盒 GGGCGG</b>）定<b>多频繁</b>，经 TFⅡD 起效',
  en:'“A eukaryotic promoter is a group of independently functioning DNA sequences lying between the transcription start site, numbered plus one, and one to two hundred base pairs upstream of it, each element seven to twenty base pairs long. Together they fix both where polymerase two starts and how often. The promoter splits into two halves. The core promoter is the minimum needed for normal initiation — the start site itself plus the TATA box at minus twenty-five to minus thirty. Acting alone it only fixes the start point and gives a basal level of transcription. The upstream promoter elements are the other half, and two are named: the CAAT box, sequence CCAAT, usually near minus seventy, and the GC box, sequence GGGCGG. Both work through TFIID, a protein complex assembled on the core promoter, and both tune the frequency of initiation while the start point stays with the core promoter.”',
  note:'<b>这一格值得画一张图</b>（书上图 8-10）。<span class="pg">p.299 p.300</span><br><b>说的时候先把两半分开再说各自管什么。</b>「从哪里」和「多频繁」是两件事、两段 DNA——这一句说出来，后面 UPE 和增强子放哪儿就都清楚了。'},

 {n:'04', t:'增强子 · 它什么都不挑，所以特异性是蛋白带的',
  ez:'“An enhancer is a D N A sequence. It markedly raises transcription of a gene linked to it. It was first found upstream of the S V forty early genes. There it was two direct repeats of seventy two base pairs. Delete both and expression drops a lot. Put one back anywhere and transcription returns. The effect is large. It is usually ten to two hundred fold. It works at any position and either orientation. Three kilobases upstream still works. Two and a half kilobases downstream still works.”',
  ezcn:'<b>增强子是能使与它连锁的基因转录频率明显增加的 DNA 序列。</b><b>它最早发现于 SV40 早期基因上游，是两个长 72 bp 的正向重复序列：两个一起删掉，表达大幅下降；只要把其中一个放回去——放在重组 DNA 上的任何位置都行——转录就恢复。</b><b>增强效应很大，一般 10～200 倍，有的上千倍。</b><b>而且与位置和取向都无关：5′→3′ 或 3′→5′ 都行，上游 3 kb、下游 2.5 kb 也照样。</b>',
  big:'⚠ <b>与位置、取向、基因都无关</b>（上游 3 kb、下游 2.5 kb 都行）· <b>10～200 倍，有的上千倍</b> · <b>却有严密的组织和细胞特异性</b> → 特异性不在序列里，<b>在蛋白里</b>',
  en:'“An enhancer is a DNA sequence that markedly raises the transcription frequency of a gene linked to it. It was first found upstream of the SV40 early genes as two direct repeats of seventy-two base pairs: delete both and expression falls sharply, put one back anywhere on the recombinant DNA and transcription returns. Cloning the human beta-globin gene onto DNA carrying those repeats raised its expression in vivo more than two hundredfold. That held whether the repeat sat three kilobases upstream of the start site or two and a half kilobases downstream. The textbook lists six properties. The effect is large, usually ten to two hundredfold and sometimes over a thousand. It is independent of position and orientation. Enhancers are mostly repeated sequences around fifty base pairs long, carrying a core that the effect requires. They have strict tissue and cell specificity. They have no gene specificity. And many respond to external signals — the enhancer upstream of the metallothionein gene answers zinc and cadmium in the environment.”',
  warn:'⚠ <b>这两条并排放，答案就自己出来了</b>：增强子<b>没有基因专一性</b>、位置取向也都不挑，<b>却有严密的组织和细胞特异性</b>。<b>既然序列本身什么都不挑，那么决定它在某个细胞里发不发力的，只能是这个细胞里有哪些转录因子——特异性是由蛋白质携带的。</b><br><b>这是这张卡上最漂亮的一处推理</b>，而且它是从书给的六条特性里读出来的，不是背下来的。<span class="pg">p.301 p.302</span>'},

 {n:'05', t:'⚠ 距离对增强子是几何问题，不是长度问题',
  ez:'“Enhancer activity depends on an odd or even multiple. The unit is five base pairs. That is half a turn of the double helix. So distance here is not about how far. It is about which face of the helix the enhancer lands on. Under the electron microscope enhancers often look like loops. The textbook gives three possible mechanisms. One is looping the D N A so enhancer and promoter meet. One is anchoring the template inside the nucleus. One treats the enhancer as an entry point into chromatin.”',
  ezcn:'<b>增强子的活性，与所涉距离是半周 DNA 双螺旋（5 bp）的奇数倍还是偶数倍有关。</b>⚠ <b>所以距离对增强子来说是一个几何问题，不是一个长度问题：要紧的是它转到了螺旋的哪一面上。</b><b>电镜下增强子常呈环状。</b><b>书给了三种可能机制：一是让双螺旋弯折成环，把增强子和启动子拉到一起；二是把模板固定在核内特定位置（例如连在核基质上）；三是增强子区充当反式因子或聚合酶Ⅱ进入染色质的「入口」。</b>',
  big:'活性按 <b>5 bp（半周螺旋）的奇偶倍数</b>变 → <b>要紧的是它转到螺旋的哪一面</b>。三种机制：<b>成环</b> · <b>固定在核基质</b> · <b>当入口</b>',
  en:'“Enhancers often appear as loops under the electron microscope. Their activity depends on whether the distance involved is an odd or an even multiple of five base pairs. Five base pairs is half a turn of the double helix. So distance here is a geometric question rather than a question of length: what matters is which face of the helix the enhancer ends up on. The textbook gives three possible mechanisms. One is bending the helix so that enhancer and promoter are brought together through protein contacts. One is anchoring the template at a particular place in the nucleus, such as the nuclear matrix. And one has the enhancer region acting as an entry point into chromatin for trans-acting factors or polymerase two.”',
  good:'<b>顺手能给的一个用法</b>：把一个带 lacZ 报告基因、加一个本身不足以启动它的基本启动子的载体整合进基因组，<b>只有插入位点附近有增强子时 lacZ 才表达</b>——于是就能读出那个增强子在什么时间、什么部位起作用。<br><b>这跟 mb-ko 上的基因捕获是同一个设计</b>：报告基因弱到只有靠外力才亮，它亮起来这件事本身就是信息。<span class="pg">p.302</span>'},

 {n:'06', t:'沉默子和绝缘子 · 同一件事的另外两个方向',
  ez:'“Two more cis acting elements stand beside the enhancer. They act on the same thing an enhancer raises. A silencer is a negative element. It lowers transcription of the gene linked to it. An insulator does something different. It blocks activation or repression from travelling along the chromosome. So it confines activity to one domain. An enhancer raises. A silencer lowers. An insulator sets the boundary.”',
  ezcn:'<b>在增强子旁边还并列着另外两个顺式作用元件，它们作用的对象跟增强子所提高的是同一件事——转录。</b><b>沉默子是负性调节元件，它降低与之连锁的基因的转录。</b><b>绝缘子做的是另一件事：它阻止激活或阻遏沿染色体传递，从而把染色体的活性限定在一个结构域之内。</b><b>增强子往上抬，沉默子往下压，绝缘子画边界。</b>',
  big:'<b>增强子抬</b> · <b>沉默子压</b> · <b>绝缘子画边界</b>（挡住激活或阻遏<b>沿染色体传递</b>，把活性限在一个结构域里）',
  en:'“Two further cis-acting elements are named alongside the enhancer, and both act on the same transcription an enhancer raises. A silencer is a negative regulatory element: it lowers the transcription of the gene linked to it. An insulator does something structurally different — it prevents activation or repression from spreading along the chromosome, and so confines a chromosome’s activity to one domain. The enhancer raises, the silencer lowers, and the insulator draws the boundary.”',
  note:'<b>绝缘子最容易被说错成「沉默子的一种」。</b>它不调高也不调低——<b>它挡的是「传递」</b>。这个区别一说出来就显得你读过书。<span class="pg">p.301</span>'},

 {n:'07', t:'⚠ 3′ 端 · 转录活性和有功能的 mRNA 是两回事',
  ez:'“Almost every eukaryotic gene carries a poly A site near its three prime end. Fifteen to thirty base pairs upstream of it lies AATAAA. That conserved sequence is required for accurate cleavage. It is required for adding the poly A tail. Now change AATAAA into AAGAAA by a point mutation. Transcription of the gene carries on as before. The processing of the transcript is blocked. So the transcript is still made. No functional messenger R N A comes out of it.”',
  ezcn:'<b>几乎所有真核基因的 3′ 端都有一个多(A)位点，它上游 15～30 bp 处的保守序列 AATAAA，对初级转录产物的准确切割和加多(A)尾是必需的。</b>⚠ <b>把 AATAAA 点突变成 AAGAAA：基因的转录活性照旧保持，mRNA 的加工却被阻断——转录产物照样做出来，却产生不了有功能的 mRNA。</b><b>所以「转录活性」和「有功能的 mRNA」是两件事，不能互相替代着说。</b>',
  big:'<b>AATAAA</b> 在多(A)位点上游 <b>15～30 bp</b>。⚠ <b>AATAAA → AAGAAA：转录照旧，加工被挡</b> → <b>转录活性 ≠ 有功能的 mRNA</b>',
  en:'“Almost every eukaryotic gene carries a poly(A) site near its three prime end. Fifteen to thirty base pairs upstream of that site lies the conserved sequence AATAAA. It is required for accurate cleavage of the primary transcript and for adding the poly(A) tail. A point mutation turning AATAAA into AAGAAA leaves the transcriptional activity of the gene intact while blocking the processing. The transcript is still made, but no functional messenger RNA comes out of it. Polymerase two does not itself terminate at the poly(A) site. Most known primary transcripts still carry half a kilobase to two kilobases of sequence downstream of it, and no single site with specific termination activity has been found. The terminator is the region at the end of a gene where transcription stops. There may be a common mechanism behind it. The terminator of the mouse beta-globin gene will terminate an adenovirus gene, and that of the Agrobacterium nopaline synthase gene terminates almost any foreign gene.”',
  warn:'⚠ <b>这一格是一刀</b>：他要是问「这个突变会不会影响转录」，正确答案是<b>不会影响转录，影响的是加工</b>。<b>把两者混起来说，就等于说不清中心法则在哪一步被挡住了。</b><span class="pg">p.301</span>'},

 {g:'关卡二 · 蛋白这一侧：反式因子', gn:'<b>三类因子 · 两个结构域 · 四种 DNA 结合域。</b>数字先说出来，后面填空就不会漏。'},

 {n:'08', t:'反式因子三类 · 第三类根本不碰 DNA',
  ez:'“Trans acting factors are the proteins that bind cis acting elements. By function they come in three classes. Basal transcription factors recognise promoter elements. Transcription regulatory factors recognise enhancers or silencers. Co factors take part without binding D N A at all. The first two classes together are the transcription factors. They split again into activators and repressors. A co factor has no D N A binding activity of its own. It works by protein protein contact. It changes the shape of a transcription factor.”',
  ezcn:'<b>反式作用因子就是结合到顺式作用元件上的蛋白质，按功能分三类。</b><b>① 基本转录因子：识别启动子元件。</b><b>② 转录调节因子：识别增强子或沉默子；前两类合称转录因子，又分转录激活因子和转录阻遏因子。</b><b>③ 共调节因子：不需要通过 DNA–蛋白质相互作用就参与转录调控。</b>⚠ <b>共调节因子本身没有任何 DNA 结合活性，它靠蛋白质–蛋白质相互作用改变转录因子的构象来起效：与激活因子协同的叫共激活因子，与阻遏因子协同的叫共阻遏因子。</b>',
  big:'① <b>基本转录因子</b>认启动子元件 · ② <b>转录调节因子</b>认增强子／沉默子 · ③ <b>共调节因子</b>⚠ <b>根本不碰 DNA</b>，靠蛋白–蛋白改构象（共激活／共阻遏）',
  en:'“Trans-acting factors are the proteins that bind cis-acting elements, and by function they come in three classes: basal transcription factors, which recognise promoter elements. Transcription regulatory factors, which recognise enhancers or silencers. And co-factors, which take part in regulation without binding DNA at all. The first two together are called transcription factors, and they divide again into activators and repressors. They recognise and bind sequences upstream of the start site or distant enhancer elements, and so decide the time and tissue specific expression of different genes. A co-factor has no DNA-binding activity of its own: it works by protein-protein interaction, changing the conformation of a transcription factor. Those working with activators are co-activators, and those working with repressors are co-repressors.”',
  note:'<b>第三类是最容易被漏掉的一类</b>，而它恰好是真核跟原核不一样的地方。<span class="pg">p.302</span>'},

 {n:'09', t:'激活因子的两个结构域 · 酵母双杂交就建在这上面',
  ez:'“A directly acting activator has two domains. The D N A binding domain gives the target site its specificity. Its particular sequence decides which promoter or enhancer this protein recognises. The transcription activation domain is the part that activates. The binding domain lands on its own sequence. It carries the activation domain along to the nearby basal machinery. Now note what that implies. The two domains are separable pieces of one protein. The yeast two hybrid system is built on exactly that.”',
  ezcn:'<b>直接起作用的激活因子有两个结构域。</b><b>DNA 结合域决定靶位点的特异性：正是这个结构域的特定序列，决定了这个蛋白识别哪个启动子或哪个增强子。</b><b>转录激活域则是负责「激活」的那一块。</b><b>DNA 结合域结合到自己的序列上，顺带把转录激活域带到附近的基础转录区域。</b>⚠ <b>而这意味着：两个结构域是同一个蛋白质上可以拆开的两块——酵母双杂交正建立在这一点上。</b>',
  big:'<b>DNA 结合域定特异性</b>（认哪个启动子／增强子）＋ <b>转录激活域负责激活</b>。⚠ <b>两块可以拆开</b> → <b>酵母双杂交</b>',
  en:'“A directly acting activator has two domains. Its DNA-binding domain is what gives the target site its specificity: the particular sequence of that domain decides which promoter or which enhancer the protein recognises. The transcription activation domain is the part that does the activating. The binding domain lands on its own sequence and carries the activation domain along to the nearby basal transcription region. An activator with no activation domain of its own can still function together with a co-activator that has one. And because the two domains are separable pieces of one protein, the yeast two-hybrid system is built on exactly that. Fuse one protein to the DNA-binding domain and another to the activation domain. When the two are pulled together, the downstream reporter gene is switched on. In the yeast three-hybrid system what pulls the two fusion proteins together is an RNA able to bind both, so the reporter reports an RNA-protein interaction instead.”',
  note:'<b>接卡 mb-int。</b>那张卡上酵母双杂交是「八法」之一；<b>这张卡讲的是它为什么可能</b>。两边对上了，这道题就是一整块。<span class="pg">p.302–304</span><br><b>三杂交那一句留着被追问再给</b>，别一口气倒完。'},

 {n:'10', t:'起始复合物 · 谁留在起始位点上',
  ez:'“Under physiological conditions polymerase two needs many partners. Over twenty protein factors form the initiation complex. Those general factors are written as T F two. T F two D and T F two B and T F two F join polymerase two first. That is the most primary complex on the promoter. Adding T F two E and T F two H completes it. Adding T F two A raises efficiency further. T F two D is built around TBP with a set of TAF proteins. As polymerase slides along the template two factors stay behind.”',
  ezcn:'<b>生理条件下，聚合酶Ⅱ转录一个基因通常要跟 20 种以上的蛋白质因子结合，形成转录起始复合物；这些通用因子写作 TFⅡ。</b><b>TFⅡD、TFⅡB、TFⅡF 与聚合酶Ⅱ在启动子上形成最初级的复合物；加入 TFⅡE 和 TFⅡH 后形成完整的转录复合物；再加入 TFⅡA 可进一步提高效率。</b><b>TFⅡD 以 TBP（TATA 区结合蛋白）为核心，加上一批 TAF（TBP 相关因子）。</b>⚠ <b>聚合酶Ⅱ沿模板滑动时，TFⅡD 和 TFⅡA 滞留在转录起始位点上，其余因子随聚合酶向 3′ 端移动。</b>',
  big:'<b>20 种以上因子</b>。TFⅡ<b>D·B·F</b> ＋ 聚合酶Ⅱ ＝ 最初级 → ＋<b>E·H</b> ＝ 完整 → ＋<b>A</b> 提效。TFⅡD ＝ <b>TBP ＋ TAF</b>。⚠ 滑动时 <b>D 和 A 留在起始位点</b>',
  en:'“Under physiological conditions, polymerase two transcribing a gene usually has to bind more than twenty protein factors to form a transcription initiation complex, and these general factors are written TFII. TFIID, TFIIB and TFIIF form the most primary complex with polymerase two on the promoter and begin transcribing messenger RNA. Adding TFIIE and TFIIH gives the complete transcription complex, which transcribes long-chain RNA. And adding TFIIA raises the efficiency further. TFIID is built around TBP, the TATA-binding protein, together with a set of TBP-associated factors, the TAFs. As polymerase two slides along the template, TFIID and TFIIA stay behind at the transcription start site. The rest move with the polymerase towards the three prime end. So the start site remains occupied by the two factors that recognise it.”',
  note:'<b>最后那一句是这一格的重点</b>：起始位点始终由认识它的那两个因子占着，所以<b>下一轮转录不必从零开始</b>。<span class="pg">p.300</span>'},

 {n:'11', t:'CTD 的磷酸化循环 · 看一个聚合酶就知道它在哪一阶段',
  ez:'“The largest subunit of polymerase two carries a repeated tail. The repeat is seven residues long. It is called the C T D. Serine two and serine five are the main phosphorylation sites. They run as a cycle through one round of transcription. At initiation serine five must be phosphorylated first. That same phosphate recruits the capping enzyme. During elongation serine five loses its phosphate. Serine two gains one instead. Serine two phosphorylation is what allows three prime processing. After transcription both are unphosphorylated again.”',
  ezcn:'<b>聚合酶Ⅱ最大亚基的羧基端带着一段 7 个氨基酸的重复序列（Tyr-Ser-Pro-Thr-Ser-Pro-Ser），这段重复区就叫羧基端结构域 CTD；第 2 位和第 5 位丝氨酸是主要磷酸化位点。</b><b>它们在一轮转录中走的是一个循环：起始阶段 Ser5 磷酸化是形成起始复合物的必要前提，同一个磷酸基还负责募集加帽酶；延伸阶段 Ser5 逐步去磷酸化、Ser2 转为磷酸化，而 Ser2 的磷酸化正是保证 3′ 加工顺利进行的东西；转录结束后两个都保持去磷酸化，有助于复合物解离，使聚合酶Ⅱ能去结合新的启动子。</b>',
  big:'<b>CTD ＝ 7 元重复</b>（Tyr-Ser-Pro-Thr-Ser-Pro-Ser）。<b>起始 Ser5</b>（顺带募集加帽酶）→ <b>延伸 Ser2</b>（保证 3′ 加工）→ <b>结束两个都去磷酸化</b>（复合物解离）',
  en:'“The largest subunit of polymerase two, at two hundred and forty kilodaltons, carries a repeat of seven residues at its carboxy terminus. The seven are tyrosine, serine, proline, threonine, serine, proline and serine. That repeated region is the carboxy-terminal domain, the CTD. Serine two and serine five are the main phosphorylation sites. Phosphorylation changes the conformation of some of the prolines, and that makes the CTD easier for other transcription-related factors to bind. The two serines run as a cycle through one round of transcription. At initiation, phosphorylation of serine five is a precondition for forming the initiation complex, and that same phosphate recruits the capping enzyme that caps the five prime end of the messenger RNA. During elongation serine five is progressively dephosphorylated while serine two becomes phosphorylated, and it is serine two phosphorylation that allows the three prime RNA processing during termination to go smoothly. After transcription both serines stay unphosphorylated, which helps the complex dissociate so polymerase two can bind a new promoter and start again.”',
  note:'<b>这是第二张该画的图。</b><span class="pg">p.301</span><br><b>落点一句话</b>：同一条尾巴在每个阶段带着不同的标记，<b>所以单看一个聚合酶分子，就知道它正处在转录的哪一个阶段。</b>这一句说出来，这一格就从背名词变成了讲道理。'},

 {n:'12', t:'四种 DNA 结合域 · 一个一个都有一句能说的话',
  ez:'“Four kinds of D N A binding domain are named. The helix turn helix has two alpha helices with a turn between them. Homeobox genes encode proteins carrying it. The homeodomain is sixty conserved residues. Its third helix sits in the major groove. Its amino terminal arm binds the minor groove. Two contact points make the binding stable. The zinc finger needs zinc to work at all. The basic leucine zipper puts a leucine every seventh residue. The basic helix loop helix must form a dimer.”',
  ezcn:'<b>四类 DNA 结合域。</b><b>① 螺旋-转折-螺旋（HTH）：一个蛋白里至少两个 α 螺旋，中间由短侧链残基形成转折；同源盒基因编码的蛋白都带 HTH，同源域是那段 60 个保守氨基酸。</b>⚠ <b>三个螺旋里第三个嵌进大沟，而 N 端的多余臂结合到小沟里——两个接触点而不是一个，结合因此才稳定。</b><b>② 锌指：只有在有锌参与时才具备转录调控活性。</b><b>③ 碱性-亮氨酸拉链（bZIP）：每第 7 个亮氨酸出现在螺旋同一方向。</b><b>④ 碱性-螺旋-环-螺旋（bHLH）：必须二聚化才有足够的结合能力。</b>',
  big:'① <b>HTH</b>：同源域 60 aa，<b>第三螺旋进大沟 ＋ N 端臂进小沟 ＝ 两个接触点</b><br>② <b>锌指</b>：<b>没锌就没活性</b>；换锌指区就换靶序列<br>③ <b>bZIP</b>：<b>拉链本身不结合 DNA</b>，碱性区才结合<br>④ <b>bHLH</b>：<b>必须二聚</b>；搭档不带碱性区就等于关掉它',
  en:'“Four kinds are named. The helix-turn-helix has at least two alpha helices in one protein with a turn between them formed by short-side-chain residues. Replacing residues in the helix nearer the carboxy terminus affects binding in the major groove. Proteins encoded by homeobox genes carry it — the MAT locus controlling yeast mating type, and the Drosophila segmentation genes antp, ftz and ubx. The homeodomain is the sixty conserved amino acids those genes encode. Of its three helices the first two lie on the outside, while the third inserts into the major groove. The extra arm at its amino terminus binds in the minor groove. That gives two contact points rather than one, and that is why the binding is stable. The zinc finger family covers fingers, twists and clusters. The number of residues between its characteristic cysteines and histidines is essentially fixed, and the domain has regulatory activity only when zinc is present. The basic-leucine zipper, bZIP, is found in the C/EBP family of liver, intestinal epithelium, fat and some brain cells. A leucine every sixth residue puts every seventh leucine on the same face of the helix, and those faces zip two helices into a dimer. The basic-helix-loop-helix, bHLH, appears in E12 and E47 and in MyoD-1, Myc and Max, and needs to form a homodimer or heterodimer to bind DNA at all.”',
  warn:'⚠ <b>bZIP 有一刀</b>：<b>亮氨酸拉链区本身并不结合 DNA</b>，真正结合的是氨基端 20～30 个富含碱性氨基酸的结构域；而不形成二聚体时，这个碱性区的亲和力明显降低——<b>所以这里的「DNA 结合结构域」实际是碱性区加拉链区合起来的整体</b>。<span class="pg">p.308 p.309</span>',
  good:'<b>两个能顺手给的实验</b>。① <b>锌指</b>：把雌激素受体的两个锌指区换成糖皮质素受体的，这个融合蛋白就<b>只结合 GRE、不再识别 ERE</b>——决定读哪一段序列的正是锌指区本身。<span class="pg">p.307</span> ② <b>bHLH</b>：异源二聚体中一方不含碱性区（如 Id 或 E12）时，该二聚体明显缺乏对靶 DNA 的亲和力——<b>给一个因子配一个没有碱性区的搭档，就是把它关掉的办法</b>。<span class="pg">p.309</span>'},

 {n:'13', t:'⚠ 转录活化域是反式因子唯一的结构基础',
  ez:'“In eukaryotes protein protein interaction makes this precise and complicated. A complete regulatory job is usually done by a complex. So not every transcription factor binds D N A directly. Having a transcription activation domain is therefore the one structural requirement. A factor that never touches D N A can still work through the complex it joins. Three kinds of activation domain are described. One is an acidic helix. One is rich in glutamine. One is rich in proline.”',
  ezcn:'<b>在真核生物中，反式作用因子的功能因蛋白质–蛋白质相互作用而变得精密复杂，完整的转录调控功能通常以复合物的方式完成——这意味着并非每个转录因子都直接结合 DNA。</b>⚠ <b>所以「是否具有转录活化域」成了反式作用因子唯一的结构基础：一个自己从不接触 DNA 的因子，仍然可以通过它所加入的复合物起作用。</b><b>转录活化域通常依赖 DNA 结合域以外的 30～100 个氨基酸残基，大体三种：带负电荷的酸性螺旋、富含谷氨酰胺的结构、富含脯氨酸的结构。</b>',
  big:'⚠ <b>有没有转录活化域 ＝ 反式因子唯一的结构基础</b>（自己不碰 DNA 也能起作用）。三种：<b>酸性螺旋</b> · <b>富谷氨酰胺</b> · <b>富脯氨酸</b>',
  en:'“In eukaryotes the function of a trans-acting factor is made precise and complicated by protein-protein interaction, and a complete regulatory job is usually done as a complex. That means not every transcription factor binds DNA directly. Having a transcription activation domain is therefore the one structural basis of a trans-acting factor: a factor that never touches DNA itself can still act through the complex it joins. The activation domain usually depends on thirty to a hundred residues outside the DNA-binding domain, and comes in three characteristic kinds. Acidic, negatively charged helices are found in the two activation domains of the mammalian glucocorticoid receptor, in Jun of the AP1 family, and in GAL4. Alone they induce initiation only weakly, and they probably work by binding a general factor in the TFIID complex or polymerase two itself and stabilising the initiation complex. Glutamine-rich domains are found in SP1, the GC-box binding protein. Its strongest of four activating regions has few polar residues but about twenty-five percent glutamine. They are also found in Oct1 and Oct2, Jun, AP2 and the serum response factor. Proline-rich domains are found at the carboxy terminus of CTF-NF1. There proline reaches twenty to thirty percent, so an alpha helix is hard to form. The same set of factors carries them again.”',
  note:'<b>这一格是这一侧的落点</b>，说完它，反式因子这一整段就收住了。<span class="pg">p.310</span>'},

 {g:'关卡一 · 包装这一侧：表观遗传', gn:'<b>两条线：DNA 上的甲基、组蛋白尾巴上的修饰。</b>它们都不改一个碱基，却决定蛋白够不够得着。'},

 {n:'14', t:'定义 · 「表观遗传」这个词说的是两件事凑在一起',
  ez:'“Epigenetic regulation happens before transcription. It works at the level of chromatin. Chromatin is the D N A and protein tangle in a eukaryotic chromosome. It has two lines. One modifies the D N A itself, which is D N A methylation. One modifies the histones, the proteins the D N A winds around. Those modifications are acetylation and methylation. Now note two things together. Not one base of the sequence changes, yet function changes. And that change can be inherited by daughter cells.”',
  ezcn:'<b>真核基因表达的表观遗传调控，指的是在转录发生之前、在染色质（真核染色体里 DNA 与蛋白质缠在一起的那种物质）这个层面上做的结构调整。</b><b>它有两条线：一是对 DNA 本身的修饰，即 DNA 甲基化；二是对组蛋白（DNA 缠绕其上的那类蛋白）的修饰，即组蛋白乙酰化与组蛋白甲基化。</b>⚠ <b>碱基序列一个都没变，功能却变了，而且这种改变还能被子代细胞继承——「表观遗传」这个词说的正是这两件事凑在一起。</b>',
  big:'转录<b>之前</b>、在<b>染色质</b>这一层做的结构调整。两条线：<b>DNA 甲基化</b> · <b>组蛋白乙酰化／甲基化</b>。⚠ <b>序列一个碱基没变 ＋ 改变能被子代继承</b>',
  en:'“Epigenetic regulation of eukaryotic gene expression means structural adjustment made before transcription, at the level of chromatin. Chromatin is the material in a eukaryotic chromosome where DNA and protein are wound together. It runs along two lines. One is modification of the DNA itself, which is DNA methylation. The other is modification of the histones the DNA winds around, which is histone acetylation and histone methylation. Two things have to be said together for the word to mean anything. Not one base of the sequence changes, and yet the function does. And that change can be inherited by daughter cells. Epigenetics is those two facts at once.”',
  note:'<b>定义里那两件事缺一不可。</b>只说「序列没变」，那是任何一种调控；只说「能遗传」，那是任何一个突变。<b>两件事凑在一起才是表观遗传。</b><span class="pg">p.311</span>'},

 {n:'15', t:'松开染色质这个动作本身就是开关 · 而且用一个核酸酶就能读出来',
  ez:'“Active transcription happens on euchromatin. That is the loosely packed part of chromatin. Heterochromatin is the densely packed part. Before transcription a region unwinds into free D N A. Only then is the structural gene exposed. Only then can factors bind the promoter region. So opening the chromatin is itself the switch. D N A ase one cuts D N A. Active genes are digested more easily than inactive ones. So one nuclease reads the open state gene by gene.”',
  ezcn:'<b>真核基因的活跃转录发生在常染色质（包装较松的那部分）上，与包装致密的异染色质相对。</b>⚠ <b>转录发生之前，特定区域会先解旋松弛成自由 DNA；把这段区域打开，结构基因才暴露出来，转录因子才能结合到启动区上——松开染色质这个动作本身就是开关。</b><b>读出来的办法是 DNase I：处于活跃状态的基因比非活跃状态的更容易被它降解。</b><b>鸡成红细胞的染色质里，β-血红蛋白基因比卵清蛋白基因更容易被切开；在鸡输卵管细胞里恰好反过来。</b>',
  big:'<b>常染色质（松）转录 · 异染色质（紧）不转录</b>。⚠ <b>松开染色质这个动作本身就是开关</b><br><b>DNase I 敏感性</b>跟着「这块组织正在转哪些基因」走 → 一个核酸酶就把开放状态<b>逐基因、逐组织</b>读出来',
  en:'“Active transcription of eukaryotic genes happens on euchromatin, the more loosely packed part of chromatin, as opposed to the densely packed heterochromatin. Before transcription, a particular region first unwinds and relaxes into free DNA. Only then is the structural gene exposed, and only then can transcription factors bind the promoter region and induce transcription. So opening the chromatin is itself the switch. Where it opens, nucleosomes are removed or altered and the local conformation changes, sometimes even from the usual right-handed form into Z-DNA. DNase I is an enzyme that cuts DNA. Genes in the active state are degraded by it more readily than inactive ones. In the chromatin of chicken erythroblasts the beta-globin gene is cut more easily than the ovalbumin gene. In chicken oviduct cells it is exactly the other way round. Sensitivity to DNase I follows which genes that tissue is transcribing, so a single nuclease reads out the open state gene by gene and tissue by tissue.”',
  good:'<b>顺手能给的第二层 · 超敏感位点</b>：活跃表达基因的染色质上一般有一个或数个 <b>DNase I 超敏感位点</b>——被切得比周围快得多的短区段，<b>大多位于基因 5′ 端的启动区</b>。果蝇 sgs4 基因上游约 330 bp 和 405 bp 处各有一个，<b>有一种突变体缺失了含这两个位点在内的约 100 bp，就再也不能合成该基因的产物</b>。鸡 β-血红蛋白基因的超敏感区在 5′ 端 −50～−280。<br><b>为什么会超敏感</b>：启动区的部分序列解开成了单链，缠不回核小体上，裸露在组蛋白表面——<b>让 RNA 聚合酶结合的正是这份暴露，让核酸酶下刀的也是它</b>。<span class="pg">p.311 p.312</span>'},

 {n:'16', t:'DNA 甲基化 · 两种酶分管「谁进来」和「传不传下去」',
  ez:'“D N A methylation adds a methyl group to a base. The main product is five methyl cytosine. Methylation switches genes off. Demethylation lets them be expressed again. In eukaryotes five methyl cytosine sits mostly in CpG. That is a cytosine followed immediately by a guanine. A methylated cytosine deaminates easily into thymine. So CpG is much rarer than base composition predicts. Where CpG occurs in runs we call it a CpG island. Housekeeping promoters are rich in CpG islands. Those islands are not methylated.”',
  ezcn:'<b>DNA 甲基化就是在碱基上加一个甲基，主要产物是 5-甲基胞嘧啶（5-mC）。</b><b>甲基化能关闭某些基因的活性，去甲基化则诱导基因重新活化。</b><b>真核的 5-mC 主要出现在 CpG 序列，即一个胞嘧啶后面紧跟一个鸟嘌呤；被甲基化的胞嘧啶极易自发脱氨变成胸腺嘧啶，所以 CpG 出现的频率远低于按碱基组成算出来的频率。</b>⚠ <b>CpG 成串出现的那段序列叫 CpG 岛；管家基因的启动区富含 CpG 岛，而这些 CpG 岛是不被甲基化的。</b>',
  big:'<b>5-mC 主要在 CpG</b>。<b>CpG 岛</b> ＝ CpG 成串那段；<b>管家基因启动区富含 CpG 岛，而且不甲基化</b><br>⚠ 两种酶：<b>从头合成型</b>决定<b>哪个基因进来</b>（慢，不需母链）· <b>日常型</b>让这个决定<b>传下去</b>（认半甲基化，亲和力高）',
  en:'“DNA methylation adds a methyl group to a base, the main product being five-methylcytosine, with small amounts of N6-methyladenine and 7-methylguanine. Methylation can switch off a gene’s activity and demethylation induces it to be expressed again, because methylation changes chromatin structure, DNA conformation, DNA stability and the way DNA interacts with protein. Its distribution is skewed: highest near the centromere, and high across most transposons, pseudogenes and small-RNA coding regions — broadly, the inactive parts of the genome. It also takes part in genomic imprinting and X-chromosome inactivation. In eukaryotes five-methylcytosine appears mostly in CpG, a cytosine immediately followed by a guanine, and because a methylated cytosine deaminates spontaneously into thymine very easily, CpG occurs far less often than base composition would predict. Where CpG occurs in runs we speak of a CpG island, and the promoter regions of housekeeping genes are rich in CpG islands which are not methylated. Two methyltransferase activities exist. The maintenance enzyme acts on hemimethylated duplexes, where the parent strand carries the methyl and the new strand does not. It has high affinity for those and rapidly methylates the cytosine opposite, so the pattern survives replication and cell division. The de novo enzyme turns unmethylated CpG into methylated CpG without any parent-strand guidance, but works slowly.”',
  note:'<b>两种酶的分工是这一格的落点</b>：<b>决定哪个特异基因落进甲基化调控之下的，是从头合成型；而让这个决定能被遗传下去的，是日常型。</b>这一句直接回答了「表观修饰为什么能遗传」的一半。<span class="pg">p.314 p.315</span>'},

 {n:'17', t:'甲基怎么起作用 · 阻断恰好在「必须接触双螺旋」那一步',
  ez:'“A methyl group works by changing the shape of the D N A. Past a certain degree of methylation the helix shifts. It goes from ordinary B D N A to Z D N A. Z D N A is contracted and its helix is deeper. The elements many proteins bind get pulled into the major groove. Then those proteins cannot reach them. So methylation lowers how efficiently factors bind the promoter region. Methylated D N A is also a poorer template in vitro. The block falls where a protein must touch the double helix.”',
  ezcn:'<b>甲基基团是靠改变 DNA 的形状来影响转录的。</b><b>甲基化达到一定程度，双螺旋会由常规的 B-DNA 过渡到 Z-DNA；Z-DNA 结构收缩、螺旋加深，许多蛋白质因子赖以结合的元件被缩进大沟里，够不着。</b>⚠ <b>所以甲基化降低了转录因子与启动区 DNA 的结合效率，带甲基的 DNA 作为体外转录模板的活性也更低——阻断恰好发生在蛋白质必须接触双螺旋的那一步。</b>',
  big:'甲基化到一定程度 → <b>B-DNA 过渡到 Z-DNA</b> → 结构收缩、螺旋加深 → <b>元件被缩进大沟里够不着</b>。⚠ <b>阻断恰好在「蛋白质必须接触双螺旋」那一步</b>',
  en:'“A methyl group works by changing the shape of the DNA. When histone H1 forms complexes with methylated and unmethylated DNA containing CCGG, the conformations differ considerably, and past a certain degree of methylation the duplex shifts from ordinary B-DNA to Z-DNA. Z-DNA is contracted and its helix is deeper, so the elements many protein factors depend on are pulled down into the major groove and cannot be reached. Methylation therefore lowers the efficiency with which transcription factors bind the promoter region, and methylated DNA is also a poorer template for RNA polymerase in vitro. The block falls exactly at the step where a protein has to touch the double helix.”',
  warn:'⚠ <b>这一格是这张卡的接缝。</b>关卡一（够不够得着）和关卡二（认不认得出）在这里接上：<b>甲基化并没有改掉任何一个元件的序列，它只是把元件放到了够不着的地方。</b><b>第 02 点那条脊梁的证据就是这一句。</b><span class="pg">p.315</span>',
  good:'<b>再往下一层 · 密度和强度的平衡</b>：与转录受抑制程度密切相关的是<b>启动区上甲基化的密度</b>。三个珠蛋白基因 CpG 密度差别很大（小鼠 α 每 50 bp 一个、人 γ 每 126 bp 一个、人 α 每 10 bp 一个）；导入 HeLa 细胞后<b>完全甲基化时三个都不表达</b>，装上 SV40 增强子后两个低密度的恢复表达，<b>高密度那个在完全甲基化时仍然不转录</b>。抑制强度与 MeCP1 结合 DNA 的能力正相关，密度越高抓得越牢。<b>所以一个启动子还转不转录，由两个量之间的平衡决定：甲基化 CpG 的密度，和启动子本身的强度。</b><span class="pg">p.315 p.316</span>'},

 {n:'18', t:'⚠ 5-mC 既是开关，也是内源性诱变剂',
  ez:'“Methylation also raises the mutation rate at that site. Five methyl cytosine deaminates into thymine. Thymine is not easily recognised by the repair system. So the site takes a heritable C to T transition. If it falls in a functional region expression is disturbed. Over a third of human transition diseases start this way. They start from methylated cytosine in CpG. So the same chemical mark does two opposite things. It switches a gene off reversibly. It rewrites the sequence permanently.”',
  ezcn:'<b>DNA 甲基化还提高了该位点的突变频率：5-mC 脱氨生成胸腺嘧啶，而 T 不易被修复系统识别和矫正，于是特定部位的 5-mC 脱氨基会在 DNA 里引入一个可遗传的 C→T 转换；若落在功能区域，就可能造成表达紊乱。</b><b>人体中由碱基转换引起的遗传病，三分之一以上源自 CpG 中胞嘧啶的甲基化。</b>⚠ <b>所以 5-mC 既是开关，也是内源性诱变剂——同一种化学修饰可逆地关掉一个基因，也永久地改写了它的序列。</b>',
  big:'<b>5-mC 脱氨 → T</b>，而 T <b>不易被修复系统识别</b> → <b>可遗传的 C→T 转换</b>。人类碱基转换遗传病<b>三分之一以上</b>源自这里',
  en:'“DNA methylation also raises the mutation frequency of the site. Five-methylcytosine deaminates into thymine, and thymine is not easily recognised and corrected by the repair system, so deamination at a particular site introduces a heritable C-to-T transition. If that site lies in a functional region, expression of the gene may be disturbed. More than a third of human genetic diseases caused by base transitions originate from methylation of a cytosine in CpG. In brain, breast and colorectal tumour cells, codon two hundred and seventy-three of p53 contains a CpG and is often mutated from CGT to CAT or TGT, arginine to histidine or cysteine. In non-small-cell lung cancer the C-to-T frequency at that site reaches fifty-nine point three percent. So five-methylcytosine is both a switch and an endogenous mutagen: the same chemical modification reversibly switches a gene off and permanently rewrites its sequence.”',
  note:'<b>这一格很好用</b>：它把表观遗传和突变连在一起，而多数人会把这两件事当成互不相干的两章。<span class="pg">p.314 p.317</span>'},

 {n:'19', t:'组蛋白乙酰化 · 中和一个正电荷就把核小体松开了',
  ez:'“A nucleosome is the repeating unit of chromatin. A histone octamer has D N A wound twice around it. Each core histone has an amino terminal tail facing outward. Those tails carry the residues that get modified. Acetylation goes onto lysines in the tail. A lysine side chain amino group carries a positive charge. The acetyl group neutralises that charge. Then the tail binds the negatively charged D N A less tightly. The nucleosome loosens. A looser nucleosome transcribes better.”',
  ezcn:'<b>核小体是染色质的基本结构单元：组蛋白八聚体外面缠着两圈 DNA，每个核心组蛋白朝外的 N 端部分叫「尾巴」——尾巴就是染色质被写字的那个面。</b><b>组蛋白乙酰基转移酶（HAT）给尾巴上的赖氨酸加乙酰基，去乙酰化酶（HDAC）再把它摘下来。</b>⚠ <b>赖氨酸侧链的氨基带正电荷，乙酰基把这个正电荷中和掉；正电荷一没，尾巴与带负电的 DNA 之间的亲和性就下降，核小体松开，转录调节蛋白也就更容易接触到染色质——乙酰化是那个「开」的标记。</b>',
  big:'<b>核小体 ＝ 八聚体 ＋ 两圈 DNA</b>，<b>尾巴是被写字的那个面</b><br><b>HAT 加乙酰基 → 中和赖氨酸正电荷 → 尾巴抓不住 DNA → 核小体松 → 开</b>；<b>HDAC 摘掉 → 关</b>',
  en:'“A nucleosome is the basic structural unit of chromatin. It is a histone octamer, two tetramers each of H2A, H2B, H3 and H4, with the DNA wound twice around it. Neighbouring nucleosomes have twenty to two hundred base pairs of linker between them. Under the electron microscope a row of them looks like beads about ten nanometres across. Histone H1 binds outside the core and stabilises the higher-order structure. The amino-terminal part of each core histone that faces outward is called the tail. The tails carry the residues that get modified. Acetyl, phosphate, methyl and ubiquitin groups go onto particular lysines and serines, for instance K9, K14, K18, K23 and K27 of H3. So the tail is the face on which chromatin is written. Histone acetyltransferase, HAT, adds acetyl groups to lysines in the tail and histone deacetylase, HDAC, takes them off. A lysine side-chain amino group carries a positive charge, and the acetyl group neutralises it. With the charge gone the tail binds the negatively charged DNA less tightly, the nucleosome shifts to a conformation that favours binding of regulatory proteins, and those proteins reach the chromatin more easily. Many transcriptional activators carry HAT activity themselves. The catalytic subunit related to transcription is a homologue of the yeast regulatory protein GCN5, which acetylates H3 and H4. TAFII250, a subunit of the TFIID complex, does the same. And the co-activators PCAF and p300/CBP do too, the latter acetylating all four.”',
  note:'<b>这一格是纯化学，所以最好背</b>：<b>正电荷被中和 → 抓不住负电的 DNA → 松开。</b>不用记哪个酶做什么，从电荷推就行。<span class="pg">p.317–319</span>'},

 {n:'20', t:'去乙酰化 · 哪些基因被沉默，由谁去募集它决定',
  ez:'“Deacetylation silences genes, and it is aimed rather than general. Yeast Rpd three and human H D A C one both work inside large complexes. Rpd three removes acetyl groups specifically. The nucleosomes then move closer together. With the co repressor Sin three it represses that promoter. The retinoblastoma protein shows the same pattern. It is a tumour suppressor bound to E two F at cell cycle promoters. Bound to E two F it recruits H D A C one. That promoter is deacetylated and its chromatin condenses.”',
  ezcn:'<b>去乙酰化使基因沉默，而且它是有指向的，并非全面铺开。</b><b>酵母的 Rpd3 和人的 HDAC1 都在很大的蛋白复合体中起作用：Rpd3 特异性地去除乙酰基，核小体随之相互靠近，再在共抑制子 Sin3 协同下抑制其所在启动子区的转录。</b><b>视网膜母细胞瘤蛋白（Rb）是一种抑癌因子，它与 E2F 类激活因子在细胞周期基因的启动子上结合；结合了 E2F 的 Rb 再把 HDAC1 募集过来，使该启动子区发生特异性去乙酰化，染色质浓缩，靶基因转录活性随之消失。</b>',
  big:'⚠ <b>去乙酰化酶复合体必须先被带到某一个启动子上才起作用</b> → <b>「哪些基因被沉默」由负责募集它的那个蛋白决定</b>（细胞周期基因这里是<b>抑癌蛋白 Rb</b>）',
  en:'“Deacetylation silences genes, and it is directed rather than applied across the board. Yeast Rpd3 and human HDAC1 both act within large protein complexes. Rpd3 specifically removes acetyl groups from histones, and the nucleosomes then move closer together. With the co-repressor Sin3 it represses transcription of genes in the promoter region where it sits. The retinoblastoma protein, Rb, is a tumour suppressor — one of those proteins whose loss releases cell division. It binds E2F-type transcriptional activators at the promoters of cell-cycle genes, and Rb with E2F bound then recruits HDAC1, so that promoter region is specifically deacetylated, its chromatin condenses, and the transcriptional activity of the target gene disappears. The deacetylase complex only works once it has been brought to a particular promoter. So which genes fall silent is decided by whatever protein does the recruiting. Here that is the tumour suppressor Rb.”',
  note:'<b>「必须先被募集」是这一格唯一要记的事</b>。它跟 mb-ko 上「Cre 装在哪个启动子下面，就决定删哪里」是同一个形状：<b>酶本身没有特异性，特异性在把它带过去的那个东西身上。</b><span class="pg">p.318 p.319</span>'},

 {n:'21', t:'组蛋白甲基化 · 同一个基团加在不同残基上，意思正好相反',
  ez:'“Lysines in the histone tail can also be methylated. What it means depends on two things. It depends on which lysine on which histone. It also depends on how many methyl groups. H three K nine me three marks constitutive heterochromatin. It is common at centromeres and telomeres. H three K twenty seven me three sits on silenced genes. H three K four me three is enriched at start sites. H three K thirty six me three runs across the transcribed region. Those last two mark active transcription.”',
  ezcn:'<b>组蛋白尾巴上的赖氨酸同样能被甲基化，而含义取决于甲基加在哪个组蛋白的哪个赖氨酸上、加了几个。</b><b>H3K9me3 常见于中心粒和端粒，标记组成型异染色质；H3K27me3 出现在沉默基因上；H3K4me3 富集在转录起始位点，H3K36me3 遍布整个转录区，两者都是转录活性区的标记。</b>⚠ <b>所以同一个化学基团加在不同残基上，意思正好相反：加在 H3 的 K9 或 K27 上是把这块区域关掉，加在 K4 或 K36 上则是标出它正在被转录。</b>',
  big:'<b>关</b>：H3<b>K9</b>me3（中心粒端粒，组成型异染色质）· H3<b>K27</b>me3（沉默基因）<br><b>开</b>：H3<b>K4</b>me3（转录起始位点）· H3<b>K36</b>me3（整个转录区）',
  en:'“Lysines in the histone tail can also be methylated, and what the mark means depends on which lysine of which histone carries it and on how many methyl groups there are. H3K9me3, trimethylation of lysine nine of histone H3, is common at centromeres and telomeres and marks constitutive heterochromatin, the part that stays condensed permanently. H3K27me3 appears on silenced genes and goes with repression of expression. H3K4me3 is enriched at transcription start sites and H3K36me3 is spread across the whole transcribed region, and both are read as marks of a transcriptionally active region. So the same chemical group means opposite things on different residues: a methyl on K9 or K27 of H3 shuts that region down, while one on K4 or K36 marks it as being transcribed.”',
  good:'<b>顺手能给的一层 · 为什么可遗传</b>：非组成型异染色质化最常见的形式是雌性体内随机失活的那条 X 染色体，它带有很高水平的 H3K27me3，而 <b>H3K27me3 上往往结合 polycomb 抑制复合物（PRC）</b>，核心成员 E(Z) 本身就是 H3K27 甲基转移酶，于是标记从成核中心<b>向周围扩散</b>。中心粒端粒一带则由 <b>HP1 识别 H3K9me2/3，再招募甲基转移酶 SUV39</b>，给邻近新组装的组蛋白打上三甲基。<br>⚠ <b>母细胞分裂时，染色质上已有的标记把相应的甲基转移酶招到新复制的 DNA 旁边，于是子代在相同位置被打上同样的标记——表观修饰之所以可遗传，靠的全部就是这一步招募。</b><span class="pg">p.320 p.321</span>'},

 {g:'收尾', gn:'落点、桥到下一张、留口子。'},

 {n:'22', t:'落点 · 三句话版',
  ez:'“Compressed into three sentences, it goes like this. Whether a gene is transcribed passes two gates. Gate one is whether a protein can reach the double helix. Chromatin packing and methylation set that. Gate two is whether it recognises what it reached. The cis elements and the available factors set that. And the two gates meet at one sentence. Methylation pulls the elements into the major groove, out of reach.”',
  ezcn:'<b>压成三句话：</b><b>① 一个基因转不转录，要过两道关卡。</b><b>② 关卡一是「蛋白够不够得着双螺旋」——由染色质包得多紧、有没有甲基决定；关卡二是「够着之后认不认得」——由有哪些顺式元件、细胞手里有哪些因子决定。</b><b>③ 两道关卡在一句话上接头：甲基化把元件缩进大沟里，蛋白就够不着了。</b>',
  big:'① 两道关卡 · ② <b>摸得到</b>（染色质、甲基化）／ <b>认得出</b>（元件、因子）· ③ 接头在<b>「元件被缩进大沟里」</b>那一句',
  en:'“Compressed into three sentences: whether a gene is transcribed in a given cell passes two gates. The first is whether a protein can reach the double helix at all, which chromatin packing and DNA methylation set. The second is whether it recognises what it has reached, which the cis-acting elements and the factors the cell owns set. And the two meet in one sentence from the textbook. Methylation pulls the binding elements down into the major groove, where the proteins can no longer reach them.”',
  note:'<b>三句话版是用来救场的</b>：他问得太大、你一时不知从哪儿进，就先说这三句，再让他挑。'},

 {n:'23', t:'桥 · 还有一层在转录之后',
  ez:'“I would add one boundary. Everything so far acts at or before transcription. There is another layer after it. R N A itself carries chemical modifications. The commonest one on messenger R N A is m six A. It has the same three parts as the histone marks. A writer complex adds it. An eraser removes it. A reader domain binds it. It changes splicing and export and stability and translation. So a gene can be turned down with its D N A untouched.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我会主动补一句边界：到此为止说的都发生在转录当时或之前，而转录之后还有一层。</b><b>RNA 自身带着化学修饰，广泛存在于 mRNA 上的一种是 m⁶A（腺嘌呤第 6 位氮上的甲基化），人和小鼠有将近 7000 种 mRNA 带这个位点。</b><b>它跟组蛋白标记是同一套三件组：写入的甲基化酶复合物（以 METTL3 为核心）、擦除的去甲基化酶（FTO、ALKBH5）、通过 YTH 结构域读取它的蛋白。</b><b>它影响剪接、核输出、稳定性和翻译——于是一个基因可以在 DNA 和染色质都没被碰过的情况下被调低。</b>',
  big:'⚠ <b>转录之后还有一层</b>：m⁶A 的<b>写（METTL3）· 擦（FTO、ALKBH5）· 读（YTH）</b>，改的是<b>剪接、核输出、稳定性、翻译</b> → <b>DNA 和染色质都没被碰过，基因照样被调低</b>',
  en:'“I would add one boundary. Everything so far acts at transcription or before it, and there is a further layer after it. Chemical modification of RNA affects the RNA’s own activity, localisation and stability. Eukaryotes carry over a hundred kinds, and only a very few are widespread on messenger RNA. N6-methyladenosine, or m6A, is methylation of the nitrogen at position six of adenine. It is one of the commoner ones, found at sites in nearly seven thousand messenger RNAs in mouse and human cells. It does not affect base pairing, which is why it was noticed early and understood late. It needs the same three parts as the histone marks: a writer, the methyltransferase complex built around METTL3. Erasers such as FTO and ALKBH5. And readers that bind it through a YTH domain with several-fold higher affinity than for unmethylated RNA. It works by changing RNA secondary structure. Methylating an adenine in a stem-loop destabilises the base pairing. The uracil-rich single strand opposite lengthens, and binding sites come closer to proteins like HNRNPC. So m6A regulates expression after transcription, affecting splicing, nuclear export, stability and translation, and a gene can be turned down with neither its DNA nor its chromatin touched.”',
  note:'<b>这一格是桥</b>：说到这里正好交给下一张卡（转录之外的每一层）。<span class="pg">p.322–326</span>'},

 {n:'24', t:'留口子 · 主动把话引到你的主场',
  ez:'“One more boundary of my own. All of this is how a cell controls its own genes. My work does the opposite thing on purpose. I put a gene under a promoter I choose. Then I keep the conditions constant. The point is to take regulation out of the picture. Only then does a difference between variants mean the protein. Otherwise it could mean the expression level. So the same machinery is a subject here and a nuisance there.”',
  ezcn:'<b>我会再补一句自己的边界：这一整套说的是细胞怎么调控自己的基因，而我的工作是<b>故意把调控拿掉</b>。</b><b>我把一个基因放在自己选的启动子下面，把条件固定住——目的就是让调控不再是变量。</b><b>只有这样，变体之间的差别才能被读成「蛋白不一样」，否则它同样可能只是「表达量不一样」。</b><b>所以同一套机制，在这里是研究对象，在我那里是要被排除掉的干扰。</b>',
  big:'细胞调控自己的基因 ↔ 我<b>故意把调控拿掉</b>（自选启动子、固定条件）→ <b>差别才能被读成「蛋白不一样」，而不是「表达量不一样」</b>',
  en:'“One more boundary of my own. All of this is how a cell controls its own genes. In my work I deliberately do the opposite: I put a gene under a promoter I choose and hold the conditions constant, precisely so that regulation stops being a variable. Only then can a difference between variants be read as a difference in the protein rather than a difference in expression level. So the same machinery is the subject here and a confounder there. That is also why a strong constitutive promoter is the usual choice for a display library.”',
  note:'<b>这一句把这张卡接到了 pe-expr 和 pe-evo 上</b>，而且用的是你真正熟的语言。<br><b>说完就停</b>，让他顺着问下去。'}
],
end:'<b>两道关卡：摸得到 · 认得出。</b>三十多个名字分两堆放，就不会串——<b>先说关卡，再说名字。</b>',

sib:[
 ['两类东西','“Cis-acting elements are DNA. Trans-acting factors are protein.”','顺式是基因自己带的序列，反式是结合上去读它的蛋白'],
 ['口令','“What brings polymerase two to this promoter.”','只有聚合酶Ⅱ转 mRNA 前体，所以一切都归到这一句'],
 ['脊梁','“Gate one is reaching. Gate two is recognising.”','摸不摸得到 ／ 认不认得出'],
 ['启动子两半','“The core promoter fixes where. The upstream elements fix how often.”','两件事由两段不同的 DNA 决定'],
 ['⚠ 增强子','“No gene specificity, yet strict tissue specificity.”','序列什么都不挑 → 特异性是蛋白带的'],
 ['增强子的距离','“Odd or even multiples of five base pairs.”','是几何问题不是长度问题'],
 ['三个方向','“An enhancer raises, a silencer lowers, an insulator draws the boundary.”','绝缘子挡的是「传递」'],
 ['⚠ 3′ 端','“Transcription carries on. The processing is blocked.”','AATAAA → AAGAAA：转录活性 ≠ 有功能的 mRNA'],
 ['第三类因子','“A co-factor has no DNA-binding activity of its own.”','靠蛋白–蛋白改构象'],
 ['两个结构域','“The two domains are separable pieces of one protein.”','酵母双杂交就建在这上面'],
 ['CTD','“Serine five at initiation. Serine two during elongation.”','看一个聚合酶就知道它在哪一阶段'],
 ['⚠ bZIP','“The zipper itself does not bind DNA. The basic region does.”','而不二聚化，碱性区的亲和力就掉下来'],
 ['表观遗传','“The sequence does not change, and the change is inherited.”','两件事凑在一起才叫表观遗传'],
 ['染色质','“Opening the chromatin is itself the switch.”','DNase I 敏感性能逐基因逐组织读出来'],
 ['两种甲基化酶','“De novo decides. Maintenance inherits.”','谁进来 ／ 传不传得下去'],
 ['⚠ 接缝','“Methylation pulls the elements into the major groove.”','阻断在「蛋白必须接触双螺旋」那一步'],
 ['乙酰化','“The acetyl neutralises the lysine’s positive charge.”','抓不住 DNA → 核小体松 → 开'],
 ['⚠ 去乙酰化','“The complex only works once it has been recruited.”','哪些基因被沉默，由募集它的那个蛋白决定'],
 ['组蛋白甲基化','“K9 and K27 shut down. K4 and K36 mark active.”','同一个基团，加在不同残基上意思相反']
],

segs:[
 {tag:'段 1 · 定义和两道关卡', h:'先说两类东西，再把两道关卡说出来，然后停',
  p:['“Transcriptional regulation in eukaryotes asks whether a given gene will be transcribed in a given cell, and two kinds of thing decide it. Cis-acting elements are DNA sequences the gene itself carries, such as a promoter, an enhancer or a silencer. They encode no product. Trans-acting factors are the proteins that bind those elements. Eukaryotes have three RNA polymerases, and only polymerase two transcribes messenger RNA precursors, so regulating a protein-coding gene comes down to one thing: what brings polymerase two to this gene’s promoter.”',
     '“I find it easiest to hold as two gates. The first asks whether a protein can reach the double helix at all, and chromatin packing and DNA methylation set that. The second asks whether it recognises what it has reached, and the cis elements plus the factors the cell owns set that. The two meet in one sentence. Methylation pulls the binding elements down into the major groove, where the proteins can no longer reach them. The block falls exactly where a protein has to touch the double helix.”'],
  note:'<b>说完第二段就停。</b>他挑哪一道关卡，你讲哪一道。<b>不要一口气把两边都铺开</b>——铺开就是三十个名字。'},

 {tag:'段 2 · 序列这一侧', h:'启动子的两半 → 增强子 → 沉默子绝缘子',
  p:['“A eukaryotic promoter is a group of independently functioning DNA sequences between the start site, numbered plus one, and one to two hundred base pairs upstream, each element seven to twenty base pairs long. It splits in two. The core promoter is the start site plus the TATA box at minus twenty-five to minus thirty. It is the minimum needed for normal initiation. Alone it only fixes where transcription starts and gives a basal level. The upstream elements, the CAAT box near minus seventy and the GC box, work through TFIID and tune how often initiation happens. So where and how often are set by two different pieces of DNA.”',
     '“An enhancer is a sequence that markedly raises transcription of a gene linked to it. It was first found as two seventy-two base pair direct repeats upstream of the SV40 early genes: delete both and expression falls sharply, put one back anywhere and transcription returns. The effect is usually ten to two hundredfold, and it is independent of position and orientation. Three kilobases upstream or two and a half kilobases downstream both work. Two of its six listed properties are worth putting side by side: it has no gene specificity at all, and yet its effect has strict tissue and cell specificity. Since the sequence itself is indifferent, what decides whether it fires in a given cell must be which transcription factors that cell has. The specificity is carried by the protein.”',
     '“Two more elements stand beside it and act on the same transcription. A silencer is a negative element that lowers transcription of the gene linked to it. An insulator blocks activation or repression from spreading along the chromosome, confining activity to one domain. And near the three prime end, fifteen to thirty base pairs upstream of the poly(A) site, sits AATAAA, required for accurate cleavage and polyadenylation. Mutating it to AAGAAA leaves transcription intact but blocks processing — the transcript is still made, and no functional messenger RNA comes out of it.”'],
  note:'<b>增强子那一段的两条特性一定要并排说</b>，那是这张卡上最漂亮的推理。'},

 {tag:'段 3 · 蛋白这一侧', h:'三类因子 → 两个结构域 → 起始复合物和 CTD → 四种结合域',
  p:['“Trans-acting factors come in three functional classes. Basal transcription factors recognise promoter elements. Regulatory factors recognise enhancers or silencers. And co-factors take part with no DNA binding of their own, working by protein-protein contact as co-activators or co-repressors. A directly acting activator has two domains. The DNA-binding domain has a particular sequence, and that sequence decides which promoter or enhancer the protein recognises. The transcription activation domain is the part that does the activating. Because those two are separable pieces of one protein, the yeast two-hybrid system is built on exactly that.”',
     '“Under physiological conditions polymerase two binds more than twenty factors to form an initiation complex. TFIID, TFIIB and TFIIF join it first on the promoter. TFIIE and TFIIH complete the complex. TFIIA raises efficiency further. TFIID is TBP with a set of TAFs. As the polymerase slides along the template, TFIID and TFIIA stay behind at the start site while the rest travel with it. Meanwhile the polymerase’s largest subunit carries a seven-residue repeat at its carboxy terminus, the CTD. Serines two and five run as a cycle. Serine five is phosphorylated at initiation and recruits the capping enzyme. Serine two takes over during elongation and allows three prime processing. After transcription both are unphosphorylated, so the complex can dissociate.”',
     '“Four kinds of DNA-binding domain are named. Helix-turn-helix is carried by homeobox proteins. Its sixty-residue homeodomain puts the third helix in the major groove and an amino-terminal arm in the minor groove. Two contact points rather than one is why it binds stably. Zinc fingers, which have regulatory activity only when zinc is present. Swapping the fingers of the oestrogen receptor for those of the glucocorticoid receptor makes the fusion bind GRE and no longer ERE, so the fingers are what decides which sequence is read. In the basic-leucine zipper, every seventh leucine lies on the same face and zips two helices into a dimer. The zipper itself does not bind DNA. The basic region does, and without dimerisation its affinity drops. And the basic-helix-loop-helix, which must dimerise to bind at all, so giving a factor a partner lacking the basic region is a way of switching it off. Above all of this: having a transcription activation domain is the one structural basis of a trans-acting factor, because a factor that never touches DNA can still act through the complex it joins.”'],
  note:'<b>四种结合域一个一个来，每个只给一句最值钱的话</b>。想全说完就一定会散。'},

 {tag:'段 4 · 包装这一侧，然后落回你的主场', h:'染色质 → 甲基化 → 组蛋白 → 留口子',
  p:['“Epigenetic regulation acts before transcription, at the level of chromatin, along two lines: methylation of the DNA itself, and acetylation and methylation of the histones. The word means two things at once — not one base of the sequence changes, and yet the change is inherited by daughter cells. Active transcription happens on euchromatin, the loosely packed part. Before transcription a region unwinds so the gene is exposed and factors can bind, so opening the chromatin is itself the switch. Active genes are more easily digested by DNase I than inactive ones. In chicken erythroblasts it is the beta-globin gene that is cut more readily, while in oviduct cells it is the ovalbumin gene. So one nuclease reads the open state gene by gene and tissue by tissue.”',
     '“DNA methylation puts a methyl on a base, mainly giving five-methylcytosine, and in eukaryotes that sits mostly in CpG. Methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine very readily, which is why CpG is rarer than base composition predicts. Where CpG runs together we speak of a CpG island, and the promoters of housekeeping genes are rich in islands that are not methylated. Two enzyme activities divide the work. The de novo methyltransferase decides which gene comes under methylation. The maintenance enzyme recognises hemimethylated duplexes, and it is what lets that decision be inherited. The methyl works by changing shape. Past a certain density the duplex shifts towards Z-DNA, contracted and with a deeper helix. The elements proteins bind are then pulled into the major groove, out of reach.”',
     '“On the histone side, a nucleosome is an octamer with DNA wound twice around it, and the outward-facing amino-terminal tails are where the marks are written. Acetylation neutralises the positive charge of a tail lysine. The tail then binds the negatively charged DNA less tightly, the nucleosome loosens, and transcription goes up. So acetylation is the open mark, and HDAC removing it is the closed one. But deacetylase complexes only work once recruited, so which genes fall silent is decided by whatever brings them: at cell-cycle promoters, the tumour suppressor Rb bound to E2F recruits HDAC1. Methylation of tail lysines means opposite things on different residues. H3K9me3 and H3K27me3 shut a region down, while H3K4me3 and H3K36me3 mark it as transcribed. And it is inherited because the existing mark recruits the matching methyltransferase to the newly replicated DNA beside it.”',
     '“I would add one boundary of my own. All of this is how a cell controls its own genes. In my work I deliberately do the opposite. I put a gene under a promoter I choose and hold the conditions constant, so that regulation stops being a variable. Then a difference between variants can be read as a difference in the protein rather than in expression level. The same machinery is the subject here and a confounder there.”'],
  note:'<b>最后一段是落点</b>：不要停在组蛋白上，把话推到「我是故意把调控拿掉的」，那是你的地方。'}
],

why:{
 rungs:[
  ['为什么调控一个蛋白质编码基因就等于「把聚合酶Ⅱ引到启动子上」？','因为真核有三种 RNA 聚合酶，而只有聚合酶Ⅱ转录信使 RNA 前体。'],
  ['为什么「从哪里起始」和「起始得多频繁」要分开说？','因为它们由两段不同的 DNA 决定：核心启动子定起始点并给基础水平，上游元件调频率。'],
  ['增强子既然位置取向都不挑，为什么还有组织特异性？','因为序列本身什么都不挑，那么决定它在某个细胞里发不发力的只能是蛋白——特异性是转录因子带的。'],
  ['为什么增强子的活性按 5 bp 的奇偶倍数变？','因为 5 bp 是半周双螺旋，所以要紧的是它转到了螺旋的哪一面——距离在这里是几何问题。'],
  ['AATAAA 突变了，为什么转录活性不受影响？','因为它管的是初级转录产物的切割和加尾，不是转录本身——转录照做，加工被挡。'],
  ['为什么共调节因子也算反式作用因子？','因为反式因子唯一的结构基础是「有没有转录活化域」，而不是「碰不碰 DNA」。'],
  ['为什么单看一个聚合酶分子就知道它在哪个阶段？','因为 CTD 上 Ser5 和 Ser2 的磷酸化在一轮转录里走一个循环：起始 Ser5、延伸 Ser2、结束都不带。'],
  ['为什么乙酰化会让转录变容易？','因为乙酰基中和了赖氨酸侧链的正电荷，尾巴抓不住带负电的 DNA，核小体就松开了。'],
  ['为什么去乙酰化酶不会把全基因组都沉默掉？','因为这个复合体必须先被募集到某一个启动子上才起作用——特异性在募集它的那个蛋白身上。'],
  ['表观修饰为什么能被子代继承？','两条：日常型甲基转移酶认半甲基化双链，把母链的模式补到新链上；组蛋白这边，已有的标记把甲基转移酶招到新复制的 DNA 旁边。'],
  ['甲基化到底挡住了哪一步？','挡住了「蛋白质必须接触双螺旋」那一步——它把元件缩进大沟里，序列一个碱基都没改。']
 ],
 stop:{lbl:'停 · 落在「阻断发生在必须接触双螺旋的那一步」',
   say:'“Below that I would be reconstructing rather than recalling. What I can say is the principle. None of these marks changes a single base of the binding element. So whatever they do, they must be doing it by changing what a protein can physically reach. That is why methylation and chromatin packing belong together, and why both act before recognition rather than instead of it.”'}
},

recog:[
 {q:'What is the difference between cis-acting elements and trans-acting factors?',
  mean:'<b>最短的问法，也是最可能的那一个。</b>答案要说清命名的依据是「怎么起作用」，不是「在哪里」。',
  ez:'“Cis acting elements are D N A sequences. The gene itself carries them. Promoters and enhancers and silencers are the examples. They encode no product at all. Trans acting factors are the proteins that bind them. Some R N As count too. The names come from how each one acts. A cis element acts on the D N A molecule it sits on. A trans factor is made somewhere and then goes and acts elsewhere.”',
  ezcn:'<b>顺式作用元件是 DNA 序列，由基因自身携带——启动子、增强子、沉默子，它们本身不编码任何产物。</b><b>反式作用因子是结合到这些元件上的蛋白质，还有一部分 RNA。</b>⚠ <b>命名的依据是「怎么起作用」：顺式元件作用在自己所在的那条 DNA 上，反式因子的产物则跑到别处去起作用。</b>',
  say:'“Cis-acting elements are DNA sequences carried by the gene itself, such as promoters, enhancers and silencers. They encode no product. Trans-acting factors are the proteins, and some RNAs, that bind those elements and thereby regulate expression. The two are named for the way they act rather than for where they sit: a cis element acts on the DNA molecule it lies on, while a trans factor is produced somewhere and then acts elsewhere. Since only RNA polymerase two transcribes messenger RNA precursors, regulating a protein-coding gene comes down to what brings polymerase two to that gene’s promoter.”',
  tail:'<b>说完就停。</b>他接着多半挑一个元件问「那是什么」,或者问「哪些蛋白」——两条都在这张卡上。'},

 {q:'What is a promoter, and what is an enhancer? How do they differ?',
  mean:'⚠ <b>这是最常考的一道对照题。</b>差别要落在<b>位置取向管不管</b>上。',
  ez:'“A promoter sits at a fixed place. It lies between the start site and two hundred base pairs upstream. It fixes where transcription starts. It also sets a basal frequency. An enhancer does not sit anywhere in particular. It works at any position and either orientation. Three kilobases upstream works. Two and a half kilobases downstream works. It raises transcription ten to two hundred fold. And it has strict tissue specificity while a promoter is general.”',
  ezcn:'<b>启动子的位置是固定的：它在转录起始位点及其上游 100～200 bp 以内，既确定「从哪里起始」，也给出一个基础频率。</b><b>增强子没有固定位置：任何位置、任何取向都起作用——上游 3 kb、下游 2.5 kb 都行——它把转录频率提高 10～200 倍。</b>⚠ <b>而且增强子有严密的组织和细胞特异性，启动子则是通用的。</b>',
  say:'“A promoter sits at a fixed place. It is a group of independently functioning sequences between the start site and one to two hundred base pairs upstream. Together they fix where polymerase two starts and give a basal frequency. Its core, the start site plus the TATA box at minus twenty-five to minus thirty, fixes the start point. The upstream elements, the CAAT and GC boxes, tune the frequency through TFIID. An enhancer has no fixed place at all. It works at any position and in either orientation, three kilobases upstream or two and a half kilobases downstream. It raises transcription ten to two hundredfold or more. There is one other difference that matters. An enhancer has no gene specificity but strict tissue and cell specificity. That tells you the specificity is carried by the transcription factors of that cell rather than by the sequence.”',
  tail:'<b>最后那半句是加分的。</b>'},

 {q:'What is epigenetic regulation?',
  mean:'⚠ <b>定义里两件事缺一不可</b>，只说一件就不是这个词。',
  ez:'“Epigenetic regulation is structural adjustment before transcription. It happens at the level of chromatin. Chromatin is D N A wound together with protein. It runs along two lines. One is methylation of the D N A itself. One is acetylation and methylation of the histones. Two things then hold at once. Not a single base of the sequence changes, yet function does. And the change is inherited by daughter cells.”',
  ezcn:'<b>表观遗传调控 ＝ 在转录发生之前、在染色质这个层面上做的结构调整。</b><b>两条线：对 DNA 本身的修饰（DNA 甲基化），以及对组蛋白的修饰（乙酰化与甲基化）。</b>⚠ <b>而且要同时成立两件事：碱基序列一个都没变、功能却变了；这种改变还能被子代细胞继承。</b>',
  say:'“Epigenetic regulation of eukaryotic gene expression is structural adjustment made before transcription, at the level of chromatin. Chromatin is the material in a eukaryotic chromosome where DNA and protein are wound together. It runs along two lines: modification of the DNA itself, which is DNA methylation, and modification of the histones, which is acetylation and methylation of their tails. The definition needs two things at once: not one base of the sequence changes and yet the function does, and that change can be inherited by daughter cells. Either fact alone would not be epigenetics.”',
  tail:'<b>他接着多半问「怎么遗传下去的」</b>——答案是两条募集机制，在这张卡上。'},

 {q:'How does DNA methylation switch a gene off?',
  mean:'⚠ <b>这一刀专门抓「甲基化把序列改了」。</b>答案要落在「形状」上。',
  ez:'“It works by changing the shape of the D N A, not the sequence. Past a certain density the helix shifts. It moves from ordinary B D N A towards Z D N A. Z D N A is contracted and its helix is deeper. The elements that factors bind get pulled into the major groove. The factors can no longer reach them. So the binding efficiency of transcription factors falls. Not one base has been changed.”',
  ezcn:'<b>它靠改变 DNA 的形状起作用，不是改序列。</b><b>甲基化达到一定程度，双螺旋由常规的 B-DNA 过渡到 Z-DNA；Z-DNA 结构收缩、螺旋加深，许多因子赖以结合的元件被缩进大沟里，够不着了。</b>⚠ <b>所以降低的是转录因子与启动区的结合效率——而一个碱基都没有被改动。</b>',
  say:'“By changing the shape of the DNA rather than its sequence. When methylation passes a certain degree the duplex shifts from ordinary B-DNA towards Z-DNA. Z-DNA is contracted and its helix is deeper. So the elements many protein factors depend on are pulled down into the major groove, where they cannot be reached. The efficiency with which transcription factors bind the promoter region therefore falls, and methylated DNA is a poorer template for polymerase in vitro as well. The block falls exactly at the step where a protein has to touch the double helix — and not a single base has been altered.”',
  tail:'<b>顺势能给的第二层</b>：抑制强度取决于启动区甲基化的<b>密度</b>与<b>启动子强度</b>之间的平衡；MeCP1 的结合能力与密度正相关。'},

 {q:'Why does histone acetylation activate transcription?',
  mean:'<b>纯化学，最好背</b>：从电荷推就行，不用背酶的名字。',
  ez:'“Acetylation goes onto lysines in the histone tail. A lysine side chain amino group carries a positive charge. The acetyl group neutralises that charge. The tail then binds the negatively charged D N A less tightly. The nucleosome shifts to a looser conformation. Regulatory proteins reach the chromatin more easily. So the transcriptional activity of that stretch goes up. H A T adds the group and H D A C removes it.”',
  ezcn:'<b>乙酰化加在组蛋白尾巴的赖氨酸上。</b><b>赖氨酸侧链的氨基带正电荷，乙酰基把它中和掉；正电荷一没，尾巴与带负电的 DNA 之间的亲和性下降，核小体转向更松的构象，转录调节蛋白也就更容易接触到染色质，这一段的转录活性随之提高。</b><b>加上去的是 HAT，摘下来的是 HDAC。</b>',
  say:'“Acetylation goes onto lysines in the amino-terminal histone tail. The amino group of a lysine side chain carries a positive charge, and the acetyl group neutralises it. With the charge gone the tail binds the negatively charged DNA less tightly, the nucleosome shifts to a conformation that favours binding of regulatory proteins, and they reach the chromatin more easily. A nucleosome made with acetylated histones is looser than one made with unmodified histones, and a looser nucleosome means higher transcriptional activity for that stretch of genome. Histone acetyltransferase adds the group, histone deacetylase removes it, and many transcriptional activators carry HAT activity themselves.”'},

 {q:'Two histone marks are both methylation. Why does one silence and one activate?',
  mean:'⚠ <b>一道很漂亮的小题</b>，答案只有一句。',
  ez:'“Because the meaning is not in the methyl group. It is in which residue carries it. It is also in how many groups there are. H three K nine me three marks constitutive heterochromatin. H three K twenty seven me three sits on silenced genes. H three K four me three is enriched at start sites. H three K thirty six me three covers the transcribed region. So the same chemical group reads as off on K nine and K twenty seven. It reads as on at K four and K thirty six.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>含义不在那个甲基上，而在「加在哪个残基上」和「加了几个」</b>。<b>H3K9me3 标记组成型异染色质、H3K27me3 出现在沉默基因上；H3K4me3 富集在转录起始位点、H3K36me3 遍布整个转录区。</b>⚠ <b>所以同一个化学基团，加在 K9 或 K27 上读作「关」，加在 K4 或 K36 上读作「开」。</b>',
  say:'“Because the meaning is not in the methyl group but in which residue of which histone carries it, and in how many groups there are. H3K9me3 is common at centromeres and telomeres and marks constitutive heterochromatin. H3K27me3 sits on silenced genes and goes with repression. H3K4me3 is enriched at transcription start sites and H3K36me3 is spread across the whole transcribed region, and both are read as marks of an active region. So the same chemical group means off on K9 and K27 and on at K4 and K36 — the mark is a position, not a substance.”',
  odd:1},

 {q:'How is an epigenetic mark inherited when the cell divides?',
  mean:'两条机制，<b>DNA 一条、组蛋白一条</b>，都落在「募集」上。',
  ez:'“Two mechanisms do it, one on each side. On the D N A side the maintenance methyltransferase recognises a hemimethylated duplex. The parent strand carries the methyl and the new one does not. It quickly methylates the cytosine opposite. So the pattern survives replication. On the histone side the existing mark does the work. H P one binds H three K nine me two or three. It then recruits the methyltransferase S U V thirty nine. That enzyme marks the newly assembled histones nearby.”',
  ezcn:'<b>两条机制，DNA 一条、组蛋白一条，而且都落在「募集」上。</b><b>① DNA 这边：日常型甲基转移酶认半甲基化的双链（母链带甲基、新链不带），迅速把对面那个胞嘧啶也甲基化，于是复制之后模式不变。</b><b>② 组蛋白这边：已有的标记自己干活——HP1 识别并结合 H3K9me2/3，再招募甲基转移酶 SUV39，给邻近新组装的组蛋白打上三甲基；PRC 复合物在 H3K27me3 上也是同一套。</b>',
  say:'“By two mechanisms, one on each side, and both come down to recruitment. On the DNA side, the maintenance methyltransferase has high affinity for hemimethylated duplexes, where the parent strand carries the methyl and the newly synthesised strand does not. It quickly methylates the cytosine opposite, so the pattern survives replication and cell division. On the histone side, the existing mark does the recruiting. HP1 dimers recognise H3K9me2 and me3 at centromeres and telomeres. They then recruit the methyltransferase SUV39, which trimethylates the newly assembled histones nearby. And polycomb repressive complexes bind H3K27me3, with the core member E(Z) itself an H3K27 methyltransferase, so the mark spreads outward from a nucleation site. In both cases the mark on the mother chromatin brings the enzyme to the same position on the daughter.”'},

 {q:'Name the DNA-binding domains of transcription factors.',
  mean:'四个，<b>每个只给一句最值钱的话</b>，想全说完一定会散。',
  ez:'“Four are named. Helix turn helix, carried by homeobox proteins. Its homeodomain is sixty conserved residues. The third helix enters the major groove. An arm at the amino end enters the minor groove. Zinc finger has activity only when zinc is present. Basic leucine zipper, with a leucine on every seventh position. The zipper makes the dimer and the basic region binds the D N A. Basic helix loop helix must dimerise to bind at all.”',
  ezcn:'<b>四个。</b><b>① 螺旋-转折-螺旋（HTH）：由同源盒基因编码的蛋白携带，同源域是 60 个保守氨基酸；第三个螺旋嵌进大沟，N 端的臂结合小沟——两个接触点，结合才稳。</b><b>② 锌指：只有有锌参与时才有活性。</b><b>③ 碱性-亮氨酸拉链（bZIP）：每第 7 个亮氨酸在螺旋同一面；拉链负责二聚，真正结合 DNA 的是碱性区。</b><b>④ 碱性-螺旋-环-螺旋（bHLH）：必须二聚化才结合得上。</b>',
  say:'“Four. Helix-turn-helix, carried by homeobox-encoded proteins such as the yeast MAT locus and the Drosophila antp, ftz and ubx genes. Its homeodomain is sixty conserved residues. Of its three helices the third inserts into the major groove, while an amino-terminal arm binds the minor groove. Two contact points rather than one is why it binds stably. Zinc fingers, a family covering fingers, twists and clusters, with a fixed number of residues between the characteristic cysteines and histidines and regulatory activity only when zinc is present. The basic-leucine zipper, bZIP, belongs to the C/EBP family. A leucine every sixth residue places every seventh on one face of the helix, and those faces zip two helices into a dimer. The zipper does not bind DNA itself. The basic region of twenty to thirty residues at the amino end does. And basic-helix-loop-helix, bHLH, in E12, E47, MyoD-1, Myc and Max, which needs to dimerise to bind DNA at all.”',
  tail:'<b>被追问「能举个证明吗」</b>：换锌指区就换靶序列（ERE → GRE），在这张卡上。'},

 {q:'How do you know a gene’s chromatin is open?',
  mean:'问的是<b>方法</b>，答案是一个核酸酶。',
  ez:'“You use a nuclease as the read out. D N A ase one cuts D N A. Genes in the active state are degraded more easily than inactive ones. In chicken erythroblast chromatin beta globin is cut more readily than ovalbumin. In oviduct cells it is exactly the other way round. So the sensitivity follows what that tissue is transcribing. Active genes also carry hypersensitive sites. Those are short stretches cut much faster than their surroundings. Most of them lie in the promoter region.”',
  ezcn:'<b>用一个核酸酶当读数。</b><b>DNase I 切 DNA，而处于活跃状态的基因比非活跃的更容易被它降解：鸡成红细胞的染色质里 β-血红蛋白基因比卵清蛋白基因更容易被切开，鸡输卵管细胞里恰好反过来——敏感性跟着「这块组织正在转哪些基因」走。</b><b>活跃基因上还有 DNase I 超敏感位点：被切得比周围快得多的短区段，大多位于基因 5′ 端的启动区。</b>',
  say:'“With a nuclease as the read-out. DNase I cuts DNA, and genes in the active state are degraded by it more readily than inactive ones. In the chromatin of chicken erythroblasts the beta-globin gene is cut more easily than ovalbumin, and in oviduct cells it is the other way round. So the sensitivity follows which genes that tissue is transcribing. Active genes also carry DNase I hypersensitive sites, short stretches cut much faster than their surroundings, and most of them lie in the promoter region at the five prime end. In Drosophila sgs4 there are two, about three hundred and thirty and four hundred and five base pairs upstream, and a mutant missing roughly a hundred base pairs containing both can no longer make the gene product. They are hypersensitive because part of the promoter sequence has opened into single strands that can no longer wind onto a nucleosome. The same exposure that lets polymerase bind is what lets the nuclease cut.”'},

 {q:'What does the CTD of RNA polymerase two do?',
  mean:'一个循环，<b>三个阶段三种状态</b>。',
  ez:'“The largest subunit carries a repeat of seven residues at its carboxy end. That repeat is the C T D. Serine two and serine five are the main phosphorylation sites. They cycle through one round of transcription. Serine five is phosphorylated at initiation. The same phosphate recruits the capping enzyme. Serine five loses it during elongation. Serine two gains one instead. That allows the three prime processing. After transcription neither is phosphorylated.”',
  ezcn:'<b>聚合酶Ⅱ最大亚基羧基端有一段 7 个氨基酸的重复序列，就是 CTD；第 2 位和第 5 位丝氨酸是主要磷酸化位点，它们在一轮转录里走一个循环。</b><b>起始时 Ser5 磷酸化（同一个磷酸基还募集加帽酶），延伸时 Ser5 去磷酸化、Ser2 转为磷酸化（保证 3′ 加工），转录结束后两个都不带磷酸，复合物才好解离。</b>',
  say:'“The largest subunit of polymerase two carries a seven-residue repeat at its carboxy terminus. The seven are tyrosine, serine, proline, threonine, serine, proline and serine. That repeated region is the CTD. Serines two and five are the main phosphorylation sites, and phosphorylation changes the conformation of some prolines, making the CTD easier for other factors to bind. They run as a cycle through one round of transcription: serine five must be phosphorylated for the initiation complex to form, and that same phosphate recruits the enzyme that caps the five prime end of the messenger RNA. During elongation serine five is progressively dephosphorylated while serine two takes over, and serine two phosphorylation is what allows three prime RNA processing during termination. After transcription both stay unphosphorylated, which helps the complex dissociate so the polymerase can bind a new promoter.”',
  tail:'<b>落点</b>：同一条尾巴每个阶段带不同的标记，所以看一个聚合酶分子就知道它在哪一阶段。'},

 {q:'Why is a co-factor still called a transcription factor if it never binds DNA?',
  mean:'⚠ <b>这道题问的是分类的依据</b>，不是某个蛋白。',
  ez:'“Because the criterion is not D N A binding. In eukaryotes a complete regulatory job is done by a complex. So not every factor in it has to touch the D N A. The one structural basis is having a transcription activation domain. A co factor has none of its own binding activity. It works by protein protein contact instead. It changes the conformation of a transcription factor. With an activator it is a co activator. With a repressor it is a co repressor.”',
  ezcn:'因为<b>判据不是「碰不碰 DNA」</b>。<b>在真核里完整的转录调控功能通常以复合物的方式完成，所以并非每个转录因子都直接结合 DNA</b>；⚠ <b>唯一的结构基础是「有没有转录活化域」——一个自己从不接触 DNA 的因子，仍然可以通过它所加入的复合物起作用。</b><b>共调节因子靠蛋白质–蛋白质相互作用改变转录因子的构象：与激活因子协同的叫共激活因子，与阻遏因子协同的叫共阻遏因子。</b>'},

 {q:'（陷阱）把绝缘子说成沉默子的一种',
  mean:'⚠ <b>两者做的是不同的事。</b>',
  ez:'“They are not the same kind of element. A silencer lowers transcription of the gene linked to it. That is a change of level. An insulator does not change the level. It blocks activation or repression from spreading along the chromosome. So it confines activity to one domain. One turns the dial down. The other draws the boundary.”',
  ezcn:'⚠ <b>两者不是一类。</b><b>沉默子降低与之连锁的基因的转录——那是改变「量」。</b><b>绝缘子不改变量，它阻止激活或阻遏沿染色体传递，从而把活性限定在一个结构域之内。</b><b>一个把旋钮拧小，一个画边界。</b>'}
],

ask:[

 {g:'术语表 · 这张卡上的名字，各是什么', gn:'形式跟 mb-ko 那张一样：<b>名字 ＝ 是什么 · 管什么 · 读出来是什么</b>。没有连接词，没有润滑。<b>先把这一层过一遍，再去读速背。</b>', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'cis-acting element and trans-acting factor',
   ez:'“A cis acting element is a D N A sequence the gene itself carries. It encodes no product. A trans acting factor is a protein that binds such an element. The names say how each one acts. A cis element acts on the D N A molecule it sits on. A trans factor is made somewhere and acts elsewhere.”',
   ezcn:'<b>顺式作用元件 ＝ 基因自身携带的 DNA 序列（启动子、增强子、沉默子），它们本身不编码任何产物。</b><b>反式作用因子 ＝ 结合到这些元件上的蛋白质。</b>⚠ <b>命名的依据是「怎么起作用」：顺式作用在自己所在的那条 DNA 上，反式在某处被做出来、跑到别处起作用。</b>',
   en:'“A cis-acting element is a DNA sequence the gene itself carries, and it encodes no product. A trans-acting factor is a protein, or sometimes an RNA, that binds such an element. The two are named for how they act rather than where they sit.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'core promoter and upstream promoter element',
   ez:'“The core promoter is the least D N A needed to start transcription normally. It holds the start site and the TATA box. The TATA box sits twenty five to thirty bases upstream. Alone it fixes where transcription starts and gives a basal level. The upstream elements are the other half. The CAAT box and the GC box are the two named ones. They tune how often initiation happens.”',
   ezcn:'<b>核心启动子 ＝ 保证聚合酶Ⅱ正常起始所必需的最少 DNA：起始位点 ＋ TATA 盒（−25～−30）。</b>⚠ <b>它单独只能定「从哪里起始」并给基础水平。</b><b>上游启动子元件（UPE）＝ 另一半：CAAT 盒（CCAAT，约 −70）和 GC 盒（GGGCGG），经 TFⅡD 调「多频繁」。</b>',
   en:'“The core promoter is the minimum DNA needed for polymerase two to start transcription normally: the start site plus the TATA box at minus twenty-five to minus thirty. Alone it fixes the start point and gives a basal level. The upstream promoter elements, the CAAT box and the GC box, tune how often initiation happens and work through TFIID.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'enhancer, silencer and insulator',
   ez:'“An enhancer is a sequence that raises transcription of a gene linked to it. It works at any position and either orientation. A silencer is the negative version. It lowers transcription of the gene linked to it. An insulator does something else. It blocks activation or repression from spreading along the chromosome.”',
   ezcn:'<b>增强子 ＝ 能使与它连锁的基因转录频率明显增加的序列，任何位置、任何取向都起作用。</b><b>沉默子 ＝ 负性的那一个，降低连锁基因的转录。</b>⚠ <b>绝缘子不调高也不调低：它阻止激活或阻遇沿染色体传递，把活性限在一个结构域里。</b>',
   en:'“An enhancer is a DNA sequence that markedly raises the transcription of a gene linked to it, at any position and in either orientation. A silencer is the negative counterpart, lowering transcription of the gene linked to it. An insulator changes neither level. It prevents activation or repression from spreading along the chromosome, confining activity to one domain.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'TFIID, TBP and the TAFs',
   ez:'“T F two D is the general factor that recognises the TATA region. It is built around T B P, the TATA binding protein. A set of T A F proteins sits with it. T A F stands for T B P associated factor. T F two D is one of the first factors on the promoter. It stays at the start site while polymerase moves away.”',
   ezcn:'<b>TFⅡD ＝ 识别 TATA 区的那个通用因子，以 <b>TBP</b>（TATA 区结合蛋白）为核心，加一批 <b>TAF</b>（TBP 相关因子）。</b>⚠ <b>聚合酶Ⅱ沿模板滑动时，TFⅡD 和 TFⅡA 滞留在起始位点上，其余因子随聚合酶走。</b>',
   en:'“TFIID is the general transcription factor that recognises the TATA region. It is built around TBP, the TATA-binding protein, together with a set of TBP-associated factors, the TAFs. It is among the first factors to assemble on the promoter, and it stays at the start site while the polymerase moves away.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'the CTD of polymerase two',
   ez:'“The C T D is the carboxy terminal domain of the largest subunit. It is a repeat of seven residues. Serine two and serine five are the main phosphorylation sites. They run as a cycle through one round of transcription. Serine five is phosphorylated at initiation. Serine two takes over during elongation. After transcription neither carries a phosphate.”',
   ezcn:'<b>CTD ＝ 聚合酶Ⅱ最大亚基羧基端那段 7 个残基的重复序列</b>（Tyr-Ser-Pro-Thr-Ser-Pro-Ser）。<b>第 2 位和第 5 位丝氨酸是主要磷酸化位点，在一轮转录里走一个循环：起始 Ser5（顺带募集加帽酶）→ 延伸 Ser2（保证 3′ 加工）→ 结束两个都去磷酸化。</b>⚠ <b>读出：看一个聚合酶分子带着哪个标记，就知道它在哪一阶段。</b>',
   en:'“The CTD is the carboxy-terminal domain of the largest subunit of polymerase two, a repeat of seven residues. Serines two and five are the main phosphorylation sites and run as a cycle through one round of transcription: serine five at initiation, serine two during elongation, and neither phosphorylated afterwards.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'the four DNA-binding domains',
   ez:'“Four kinds are named. Helix turn helix carries a homeodomain of sixty conserved residues. Its third helix enters the major groove. An arm at its amino end enters the minor groove. A zinc finger has activity only when zinc is present. A basic leucine zipper puts a leucine on every seventh position. A basic helix loop helix must form a dimer to bind at all.”',
   ezcn:'<b>四类。</b><b>① 螺旋-转折-螺旋（HTH）</b>：同源域 60 个保守氨基酸；<b>第三个螺旋嵌进大沟，N 端的臂结合小沟——两个接触点，所以稳</b>。<b>② 锰指</b>：只有有锰参与时才有活性。<b>③ 碱性-亮氨酸拉链（bZIP）</b>：每第 7 个亮氨酸在螺旋同一面；拉链本身不结合 DNA，碱性区才结合。<b>④ 碱性-螺旋-环-螺旋（bHLH）</b>：必须二聚化才结合得上。',
   en:'“Four are named. Helix-turn-helix, carried by homeobox proteins, whose sixty-residue homeodomain puts its third helix in the major groove and an amino-terminal arm in the minor groove. Zinc fingers, active only when zinc is present. The basic-leucine zipper, where the zipper makes the dimer and the basic region binds the DNA. And the basic-helix-loop-helix, which must dimerise to bind at all.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'transcription activation domain',
   ez:'“A transcription activation domain is the part of a factor that does the activating. It sits outside the D N A binding domain. Having one is the single structural requirement for a trans acting factor. A factor that never touches D N A can still work through a complex. Three kinds are described. An acidic helix, a glutamine rich region, and a proline rich region.”',
   ezcn:'<b>转录活化域 ＝ 因子身上负责「激活」的那一块，在 DNA 结合域之外，通常靠 30～100 个残基。</b>⚠ <b>「有没有转录活化域」是反式作用因子唯一的结构基础——一个自己从不接触 DNA 的因子，仍然可以通过它所加入的复合物起作用。</b><b>三种：酸性螺旋 · 富谷氨酰胺 · 富脯氨酸。</b>',
   en:'“A transcription activation domain is the part of a factor that does the activating, lying outside the DNA-binding domain and usually depending on thirty to a hundred residues. Having one is the single structural basis of a trans-acting factor, so a factor that never touches DNA can still act through the complex it joins.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'euchromatin, heterochromatin and the nucleosome',
   ez:'“Euchromatin is the loosely packed part of chromatin. Active transcription happens there. Heterochromatin is the densely packed part. A nucleosome is the repeating unit of chromatin. It is a histone octamer with D N A wound twice around it. The amino terminal tails face outward. Those tails carry the residues that get modified.”',
   ezcn:'<b>常染色质 ＝ 包装较松的那部分，活跃转录就发生在这里；异染色质 ＝ 包装致密的那部分。</b><b>核小体 ＝ 染色质的重复单元：组蛋白八聚体外面缠着两圈 DNA，相邻之间 20～200 bp 间隔。</b>⚠ <b>每个核心组蛋白朝外的 N 端叫「尾巴」——那就是染色质被写字的那个面。</b>',
   en:'“Euchromatin is the loosely packed part of chromatin, where active transcription happens, and heterochromatin is the densely packed part. A nucleosome is the repeating unit of chromatin, a histone octamer with the DNA wound twice around it. The amino-terminal tails of the core histones face outward and carry the residues that get modified.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'DNase I sensitivity and hypersensitive sites',
   ez:'“D N A ase one is an enzyme that cuts D N A. Genes in the active state are degraded by it more readily. So its sensitivity follows what that tissue is transcribing. A hypersensitive site is a short stretch cut much faster than its surroundings. Most of them lie in the promoter region. They are exposed because part of the sequence has opened into single strands.”',
   ezcn:'<b>DNase I 敏感性 ＝ 用一个核酸酶读「染色质开不开」：活跃的基因比非活跃的更容易被降解，而且敏感性跟着「这块组织正在转哪些基因」走。</b><b>超敏感位点 ＝ 被切得比周围快得多的短区段，大多在 5′ 启动区。</b>⚠ <b>它们超敏感，是因为那段序列解开成了单链、缠不回核小体上——让聚合酶结合的正是这份暴露。</b>',
   en:'“DNase I is an enzyme that cuts DNA, and genes in the active state are degraded by it more readily than inactive ones, so its sensitivity follows which genes a tissue is transcribing. A hypersensitive site is a short stretch cut much faster than its surroundings, usually in the promoter region, exposed because part of the sequence has opened into single strands.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'CpG and the CpG island',
   ez:'“CpG is a cytosine immediately followed by a guanine. Five methyl cytosine sits mostly there. A CpG island is a stretch where CpG occurs in runs. CpG is otherwise rare in the genome. A methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine very readily. The promoters of housekeeping genes are rich in CpG islands. Those islands are not methylated.”',
   ezcn:'<b>CpG ＝ 一个胞嘧啶后面紧跟一个鸟嘌呤；真核的 5-甲基胞嘧啶主要出现在这里。</b><b>CpG 岛 ＝ CpG 成串出现的那段序列。</b>⚠ <b>基因组里 CpG 本来很少，因为被甲基化的胞嘧啶极易自发脱氨变成胸腺嘧啶。管家基因的启动区富含 CpG 岛，而这些 CpG 岛是不被甲基化的。</b>',
   en:'“CpG is a cytosine immediately followed by a guanine, and five-methylcytosine sits mostly there. A CpG island is a stretch where CpG occurs in runs. CpG is otherwise rarer than base composition predicts, because a methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine very readily. Housekeeping promoters are rich in CpG islands, and those islands are not methylated.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'maintenance and de novo methyltransferase',
   ez:'“Two methyltransferase activities exist. The maintenance enzyme acts on a half methylated duplex. The parent strand carries the methyl and the new strand does not. It methylates the cytosine opposite, so the pattern survives replication. The de novo enzyme methylates unmethylated CpG. It needs no parent strand to copy, but it works slowly.”',
   ezcn:'<b>两种甲基化酶活性。</b><b>日常型（maintenance）：作用于半甲基化的双链（母链带甲基、新链不带），把对面那个胞嘧啶也甲基化，于是复制之后模式不变。</b><b>从头合成型（de novo）：把未甲基化的 CpG 变成 mCpG，不需母链指导，但很慢。</b>⚠ <b>分工：从头合成型决定「哪个基因进来」，日常型让这个决定「传得下去」。</b>',
   en:'“Two methyltransferase activities exist. The maintenance enzyme acts on hemimethylated duplexes, where the parent strand carries the methyl and the new strand does not. It methylates the cytosine opposite, so the pattern survives replication. The de novo enzyme turns unmethylated CpG into methylated CpG without parent-strand guidance, but works slowly.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'HAT and HDAC',
   ez:'“H A T is histone acetyltransferase. It adds an acetyl group to a lysine in the histone tail. H D A C is histone deacetylase. It takes that group off. A lysine side chain carries a positive charge. The acetyl neutralises it, so the tail grips the D N A less tightly. The nucleosome loosens and transcription goes up.”',
   ezcn:'<b>HAT ＝ 组蛋白乙酰基转移酶，给尾巴上的赖氨酸加乙酰基；HDAC ＝ 去乙酰化酶，把它摘下来。</b>⚠ <b>机制是电荷：赖氨酸侧链带正电荷，乙酰基把它中和掉，尾巴就抓不住带负电的 DNA，核小体松开，转录活性提高。</b><b>乙酰化是那个「开」的标记。</b>',
   en:'“HAT is histone acetyltransferase, which adds an acetyl group to a lysine in the histone tail, and HDAC is histone deacetylase, which takes it off. The mechanism is charge: a lysine side chain carries a positive charge, the acetyl neutralises it, the tail grips the negatively charged DNA less tightly, and the nucleosome loosens.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'the histone methylation marks',
   ez:'“Histone marks are written as histone, residue, and number of methyls. H three K nine me three marks constitutive heterochromatin. H three K twenty seven me three sits on silenced genes. H three K four me three is enriched at start sites. H three K thirty six me three covers the transcribed region. So the same group means off on some residues and on at others.”',
   ezcn:'<b>组蛋白标记的写法 ＝ 哪个组蛋白 ＋ 哪个残基 ＋ 几个甲基。</b><b>关：H3K9me3（中心粒端粒，组成型异染色质）· H3K27me3（沉默基因）。</b><b>开：H3K4me3（转录起始位点）· H3K36me3（整个转录区）。</b>⚠ <b>同一个化学基团，加在不同残基上意思正好相反。</b>',
   en:'“A histone mark is written as the histone, the residue and the number of methyl groups. H3K9me3 and H3K27me3 shut a region down, while H3K4me3 and H3K36me3 mark it as transcribed. The same chemical group means opposite things on different residues.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'HKMT, PRMT and the SET domain',
   ez:'“Lysine and arginine are the two residues that can be methylated. So the transferases come in two classes. Histone lysine methyltransferases carry a S E T domain. Protein arginine methyltransferases are the other class. How many methyls one can add is set by the shape of its catalytic centre.”',
   ezcn:'<b>能被甲基化的残基有两种（赖氨酸、精氨酸），所以甲基转移酶也分两类：<b>HKMT</b>（组蛋白赖氨酸甲基转移酶，几乎都带一个 <b>SET 结构域</b>作为催化区）和 <b>PRMT</b>（蛋白质精氨酸甲基转移酶）。</b>⚠ <b>能加几个甲基，由催化中心的空间位阻决定。</b>',
   en:'“Lysine and arginine are the two residues that can be methylated, so the transferases fall into two classes. Histone lysine methyltransferases almost all carry a SET domain as their catalytic region. Protein arginine methyltransferases are the other class. How many methyl groups one can add is decided by the steric hindrance at its catalytic centre.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'HP1, PRC and how a mark is inherited',
   ez:'“H P one binds the mark H three K nine me two or three. It then recruits the methyltransferase S U V thirty nine. A polycomb repressive complex binds H three K twenty seven me three. Its core member is itself a methyltransferase for that residue. So an existing mark brings the enzyme to the newly copied D N A beside it. That recruitment is the whole of the inheritance.”',
   ezcn:'<b>HP1 ＝ 识别并结合 H3K9me2/3 的蛋白，再招募甲基转移酶 SUV39。</b><b>PRC（polycomb 抑制复合物）＝ 结合 H3K27me3 的复合物，核心成员 E(Z) 本身就是 H3K27 甲基转移酶。</b>⚠ <b>这就是表观修饰可遗传的全部机制：已有的标记把酶招到新复制的 DNA 旁边，子代在相同位置被打上同样的标记。</b>',
   en:'“HP1 binds the H3K9me2 and me3 marks and recruits the methyltransferase SUV39. A polycomb repressive complex binds H3K27me3, and its core member is itself a methyltransferase for that residue. So an existing mark brings the matching enzyme to the newly replicated DNA beside it, and that recruitment is the whole of the inheritance.”'},
  {r:'高', q:'m6A and its writer, eraser and reader',
   ez:'“m six A is methylation of the nitrogen at position six of adenine. It sits on messenger R N A. It needs three parts. A writer complex adds it, built around M E T T L three. Erasers remove it, F T O and A L K B H five. Readers bind it through a Y T H domain. It changes splicing and export and stability and translation.”',
   ezcn:'<b>m⁶A ＝ mRNA 上腺嘌呤第 6 位氮原子的甲基化。</b><b>它需要三件组：<b>写</b>（以 METTL3 为核心的甲基化酶复合物）· <b>擦</b>（FTO、ALKBH5）· <b>读</b>（通过 YTH 结构域）。</b>⚠ <b>它影响剪接、核输出、稳定性和翻译——于是一个基因可以在 DNA 和染色质都没被碰过的情况下被调低。</b>',
   en:'“m6A is methylation of the nitrogen at position six of adenine, found on messenger RNA. It needs three parts: a writer complex built around METTL3, erasers such as FTO and ALKBH5, and readers that bind it through a YTH domain. It affects splicing, nuclear export, stability and translation.”'},
 ]},
 {g:'定义类', gn:'他挑一个词问「那是什么」。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'What is the core promoter?',
   ez:'“The core promoter is the minimum D N A needed for normal initiation. It is the part polymerase two cannot do without. It contains the transcription start site itself. It also contains the TATA box. The TATA box lies twenty five to thirty base pairs upstream. Acting alone the core promoter fixes where transcription starts. It gives only a basal level of transcription.”',
   ezcn:'<b>核心启动子 ＝ 保证 RNA 聚合酶Ⅱ正常起始转录所必需的最少 DNA 序列</b>：<b>包括转录起始位点本身，以及位于起始位点上游 −25～−30 bp 处的 TATA 盒。</b><b>它单独起作用时，只能确定转录起始位点并产生基础水平的转录。</b>',
   en:'“The core promoter is the minimum DNA sequence needed for RNA polymerase two to initiate transcription normally: the transcription start site itself, plus the TATA box at minus twenty-five to minus thirty. Acting alone it fixes where transcription starts and gives only a basal level. How often initiation happens is set by the other half of the promoter, the upstream elements.”'},

  {r:'高', q:'What is an upstream promoter element?',
   ez:'“The upstream promoter elements are the other half of a promoter. Two of them are named. The CAAT box has the sequence CCAAT. It usually lies near minus seventy. The GC box has the sequence GGGCGG. Both act through T F two D. That is a protein complex assembled on the core promoter. They tune how often initiation happens. The start point still belongs to the core promoter.”',
   ezcn:'<b>上游启动子元件（UPE）是启动子的另一半，其中两个是：CAAT 盒（序列 CCAAT，通常位于 −70 bp 附近）和 GC 盒（序列 GGGCGG）。</b><b>两者都通过 TFⅡD——一个装配在核心启动子上的蛋白质复合物——来调节转录起始的频率、提高转录效率，而起始点仍然由核心启动子说了算。</b>',
   en:'“The upstream promoter elements are the other half of a promoter, and two are named: the CAAT box, sequence CCAAT, usually near minus seventy, and the GC box, sequence GGGCGG. Both work through TFIID, a protein complex assembled on the core promoter, to tune the frequency of initiation and raise transcriptional efficiency. The start point itself stays with the core promoter.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'What is a CpG island?',
   ez:'“CpG is a cytosine followed immediately by a guanine. In eukaryotes five methyl cytosine sits mostly there. A CpG island is a stretch where CpG occurs in runs. CpG is otherwise rare in the genome. A methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine very easily. That is why the frequency is lower than predicted. The promoters of housekeeping genes are rich in CpG islands. Those islands are not methylated.”',
   ezcn:'<b>CpG ＝ 一个胞嘧啶后面紧跟一个鸟嘌呤；真核的 5-甲基胞嘧啶主要出现在这里。</b><b>CpG 岛 ＝ CpG 成串出现的那段序列。</b><b>基因组里 CpG 本来很少，因为被甲基化的胞嘧啶极易自发脱氨变成胸腺嘧啶，所以它出现的频率远低于按碱基组成算出来的。</b>⚠ <b>管家基因的启动区富含 CpG 岛，而这些 CpG 岛是不被甲基化的。</b>',
   en:'“CpG is a cytosine immediately followed by a guanine, and in eukaryotes five-methylcytosine sits mostly there. A CpG island is a stretch where CpG occurs in runs. CpG is otherwise rarer in the genome than base composition predicts, because a methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine very readily. The promoter regions of housekeeping genes are rich in CpG islands, and those islands are not methylated.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Are there kinds of regulation that change the DNA itself?',
   ez:'“Yes, and the textbook separates them from the rest. Transcriptional and translational control leave the genome alone. This class does not. It works by gene loss, gene amplification, gene rearrangement and transposition. Amplification means the copy number of certain genes rises sharply. A Xenopus oocyte starts with about five hundred ribosomal R N A genes. By the diplotene stage it has about two million. That is an amplification of nearly four thousandfold. It is enough for ten to the twelfth ribosomes.”',
   ezcn:'<b>有，而且书把这一类跟别的分开：转录水平和翻译水平的调控并不动基因组本身，而这一类直接改动 DNA 模板——基因丢失、基因扩增、基因重排和移位。</b><b>基因扩增指某些基因的拷贝数专一性地大量增加：非洲爪蟾卵母细胞原本约有 500 个 rRNA 基因拷贝，到减数分裂 I 的双线期已增至约 200 万个，扩增近 4000 倍，足够合成 10¹² 个核糖体。</b>⚠ <b>这是一场有期限的临时扩产：卵母细胞一旦成熟，多余的 rDNA 就被逐渐降解，等分裂到几百个细胞时过剩现象已完全消失。</b>',
   en:'“Yes, and the textbook keeps this class separate from the others, because transcriptional and translational control leave the genome itself untouched while this one does not. It works by gene loss, gene amplification, gene rearrangement and transposition. Amplification means the copy number of particular genes rises sharply and specifically. A Xenopus oocyte begins with about five hundred copies of the ribosomal RNA genes. By the diplotene stage of the first meiotic division it has about two million. That is an amplification of nearly four thousandfold, enough for ten to the twelfth ribosomes during cleavage and embryogenesis. It is a temporary expansion with an end date. Once the oocyte matures the surplus ribosomal DNA is progressively degraded, and by a few hundred cells the excess has gone entirely.”'},
  {r:'中', q:'What is gene rearrangement, and where does it matter?',
   ez:'“Gene rearrangement moves a gene closer to a promoter. That move is what starts its transcription. Immunoglobulin genes are the standard case. The human heavy chain locus sits on chromosome fourteen. It holds eighty six V segments and thirty D segments. It also holds nine J segments and eleven C segments. In an embryonic cell those lie far apart. As a B lymphocyte differentiates, recombination joins one of each. The result is a single gene that can be expressed.”',
   ezcn:'<b>基因重排 ＝ 把一个基因从远离启动子的地方挪到紧挨启动子的位置，从而启动它的转录。</b><b>免疫球蛋白基因是标准例子：人 14 号染色体上的重链基因座带有 86 个 V 片段、30 个 D 片段、9 个 J 片段和 11 个 C 片段，在胚胎细胞中彼此相隔很远；B 淋巴细胞分化时，染色体内 DNA 重组把四类片段各取其一连成一个有表达活性的基因。</b>⚠ <b>人珠蛋白基因家族靠同一类事件换挡：间隔序列 S₁ 缺失使调节基因与受体基因相连、转录出 ε 链，S₂ 缺失在胚胎 3～9 个月转录出 γ 链，出生后 S₃ 缺失激活 β 与 δ。</b>',
   en:'“Gene rearrangement means moving a gene from a position far from a promoter to one right beside it, and that move is what starts its transcription. Immunoglobulin genes are the standard example. The human heavy chain locus IGH on chromosome fourteen carries eighty-six V segments, thirty D segments, nine J segments and eleven C segments, lying far apart in an embryonic cell. As a B lymphocyte differentiates, recombination within the chromosome joins one segment of each kind into a single gene with expression activity. The human globin family changes gear by the same kind of event. Loss of the spacer S one links a regulatory gene to a receptor gene, so the neighbouring structural gene transcribes the epsilon chain. Loss of S two gives the gamma chain from the third to the ninth month. And after birth loss of S three activates beta and delta.”'},
  {r:'中', q:'What is a nucleosome, and what is a histone tail?',
   ez:'“A nucleosome is the repeating unit of chromatin. A histone octamer sits at its centre. That octamer is two tetramers. Each holds H two A and H two B and H three and H four. D N A winds twice around it. Neighbouring nucleosomes have twenty to two hundred base pairs between them. Histone H one binds outside the core and stabilises the structure. The tail is the amino terminal part of each core histone. It faces outward and carries the modified residues.”',
   ezcn:'<b>核小体 ＝ 染色质的基本结构单元：由组蛋白八聚体（两个各含 H2A、H2B、H3、H4 的四聚体）与缠绕其上两圈的 DNA 组成，相邻核小体之间有 20～200 bp 间隔；电镜下像一串珠子，每颗直径约 10 nm。</b><b>H1 结合在核心之外，稳定核小体序列和染色质高级结构。</b><b>尾巴 ＝ 每个核心组蛋白朝向外部的 N 端部分——乙酰基、磷酸基、甲基、泛素就加在这上面指定的赖氨酸和丝氨酸上。</b>',
   en:'“A nucleosome is the basic repeating unit of chromatin. It is a histone octamer, two tetramers each of H2A, H2B, H3 and H4, with the DNA wound twice around it and twenty to two hundred base pairs of linker between neighbours. Under the electron microscope a row of them looks like beads about ten nanometres across. Histone H1 binds outside the core and stabilises the higher-order structure. The tail is the amino-terminal part of each core histone that faces outward, and it carries the residues that get modified, such as K9, K14, K18, K23 and K27 of H3.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Which enzymes write and erase histone methylation?',
   ez:'“Two residues can be methylated, lysine and arginine. So the transferases come in two classes. Histone lysine methyltransferases carry a S E T domain. Protein arginine methyltransferases are the other class. How many methyl groups one can add is set by shape. The steric hindrance at its catalytic centre decides it. D I M five makes mono, di and trimethyl H three K nine. S E T seven nine makes only monomethyl H three K four. Swap their core residues and the two abilities swap too.”',
   ezcn:'<b>组蛋白上能被甲基化的残基有两种——赖氨酸和精氨酸——所以甲基转移酶也分两类：组蛋白赖氨酸甲基转移酶（HKMT，几乎都带一个 SET 结构域作为催化活性区），以及蛋白质精氨酸甲基转移酶（PRMT）。</b>⚠ <b>一个 HKMT 能加几个甲基，由其催化中心几个关键氨基酸构成的空间位阻决定：DIM5 能催化 H3K9 的单、双、三甲基化，而 SET7/9 只能催化 H3K4 的单甲基化；把两者相应的核心氨基酸互换，这两种能力也跟着互换。</b>',
   en:'“Two residues on a histone can be methylated, lysine and arginine, so the methyltransferases fall into two classes. The histone lysine methyltransferases almost all carry a catalytic region called the SET domain. The protein arginine methyltransferases are the other class. How many methyl groups one of them can add is decided by the steric hindrance built from a few key amino acids at its catalytic centre. DIM5 can catalyse mono, di and trimethylation of H3K9, while SET7 nine can catalyse only monomethylation of H3K4. Swapping the corresponding core residues between them swaps those abilities too.”'},
  {r:'中', q:'Can histone methylation be removed again?',
   ez:'“Yes, though it was long thought to be permanent. Demethylases were only found after two thousand and two. L S D one was the first lysine demethylase. It uses F A D as its cofactor. It removes mono and dimethyl from H three K four. Many other enzymes carry a jumonji domain. That domain can take off a trimethyl group. And one demethylase can work in both directions. Its partner decides which.”',
   ezcn:'<b>能，虽然人们很长一段时间认为组蛋白甲基化是稳定存在的——2002 年以后才逐渐发现去甲基化酶。</b><b>最早的赖氨酸去甲基化酶是 LSD1，以 FAD 为辅助因子，催化 H3K4me1/2 的去甲基化；而 JMJD2 等许多酶所带的 jumonji 结构域，是能脱掉三甲基的催化活性区。</b>⚠ <b>同一个去甲基化酶是激活还是抑制转录，取决于跟它搭档的是谁：LSD1 与 Co-REST 抑制复合物结合时催化 H3K4me1/2 的去甲基化，与雄激素受体结合时催化 H3K9 的去甲基化。</b>',
   en:'“Yes, although for a long time histone methylation was thought to be stable, and demethylases were only found from two thousand and two onwards. The first lysine-specific demethylase was LSD1, which uses FAD as its cofactor and catalyses demethylation of H3K4 monomethyl and dimethyl. Many other enzymes, JMJD2 among them, carry a jumonji domain, and that domain is the catalytic region able to take off a trimethyl group. One demethylase can work in either direction depending on its partner. Bound to the Co-REST repressive complex, LSD1 demethylates H3K4 monomethyl and dimethyl. Bound to the androgen receptor, it demethylates H3K9 instead.”'},
  {r:'中', q:'What is euchromatin and what is heterochromatin?',
   ez:'“Euchromatin is the loosely packed part of chromatin. Active transcription of eukaryotic genes happens there. Heterochromatin is the densely packed part. Constitutive heterochromatin stays condensed permanently. Centromeres and telomeres are the usual examples. They carry the mark H three K nine me three. The randomly inactivated X chromosome is the other kind. It carries high levels of H three K twenty seven me three.”',
   ezcn:'<b>常染色质 ＝ 染色质中包装较松的那部分，真核基因的活跃转录就发生在这里；异染色质 ＝ 包装致密的那部分。</b><b>组成型异染色质长期保持致密，典型是中心粒和端粒，带 H3K9me3 标记。</b><b>非组成型的典型是雌性体内随机失活的那条 X 染色体，带很高水平的 H3K27me3。</b>',
   en:'“Euchromatin is the loosely packed part of chromatin, and active transcription of eukaryotic genes happens there. Heterochromatin is the densely packed part. Constitutive heterochromatin stays condensed permanently, and centromeres and telomeres are the usual examples, marked by H3K9me3. The other kind is not constitutive. The best-known case is the X chromosome randomly inactivated in females, which carries high levels of H3K27me3 with polycomb repressive complexes bound to it.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'What are the three kinds of transcription activation domain?',
   ez:'“Three are described, and each is named by what it is rich in. The first is an acidic negatively charged helix. The glucocorticoid receptor and Jun and GAL four have one. Alone it induces initiation only weakly. The second is rich in glutamine. In S P one the strongest activating region is about a quarter glutamine. The third is rich in proline. The carboxy end of C T F N F one reaches twenty to thirty percent.”',
   ezcn:'<b>三种，各以「富含什么」得名。</b><b>① 带负电荷的酸性螺旋：糖皮质激素受体的两个转录活化域、AP1 家族的 Jun、GAL4 都属此类；它单独诱导起始的活性并不强，可能是与 TFⅡD 里某个通用因子或聚合酶Ⅱ结合，起稳定起始复合物的作用。</b><b>② 富含谷氨酰胺：SP1 四个活化区里最强的那个，谷氨酰胺约占 25%。</b><b>③ 富含脯氨酸：CTF–NF1 的羧基端达 20%～30%，很难形成 α 螺旋。</b>',
   en:'“Three are described, each named for what it is rich in. Acidic, negatively charged helices are found in the two activation domains of the mammalian glucocorticoid receptor, in Jun of the AP1 family and in GAL4. Alone they induce initiation only weakly, and they probably work by binding a general factor in the TFIID complex or polymerase two itself and stabilising the initiation complex. Glutamine-rich domains are found in SP1. Its strongest of four activating regions has few polar residues but about twenty-five percent glutamine. They are also found in Oct1 and Oct2, Jun, AP2 and the serum response factor. Proline-rich domains are found at the carboxy terminus of CTF-NF1, where proline reaches twenty to thirty percent, so an alpha helix is hard to form.”'}
 ]},

 {g:'为什么类', gn:'他问「为什么会这样」。这一组是这张卡最该答得好的。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'Why must the specificity of an enhancer be carried by proteins?',
   ez:'“Because the sequence itself is indifferent to everything. An enhancer works at any position and either orientation. It works three kilobases upstream or downstream. And it has no gene specificity at all. It shows its effect on different gene combinations. Yet its effect has strict tissue and cell specificity. Something must supply that specificity. The sequence cannot, since it ignores position and gene. So it has to be the transcription factors that cell owns.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>序列本身对什么都不挑</b>：增强子在任何位置、任何取向下都起作用，上游 3 kb、下游 2.5 kb 都行，而且<b>没有基因专一性</b>，可以在不同的基因组合上表现增强效应。<b>可它的效应却有严密的组织和细胞特异性。</b>⚠ <b>那么这份特异性只能由别的东西提供——既然序列不挑，就只能是这个细胞里恰好有哪些转录因子。特异性是由蛋白质携带的。</b>',
   en:'“Because the sequence itself is indifferent to everything that could carry specificity. An enhancer works at any position and in either orientation, three kilobases upstream or two and a half kilobases downstream. It has no gene specificity at all, and shows its effect on different gene combinations. Yet its effect does have strict tissue and cell specificity. Since the sequence ignores position, orientation and gene, whatever supplies that specificity has to be something else, and the only candidate is which transcription factors the cell happens to own.”'},

  {r:'高', q:'Why do methylation and chromatin packing belong together?',
   ez:'“Because they block at the same step. Neither one changes a base of the binding element. So neither can be changing what the protein recognises. What they change is what a protein can physically reach. Packing hides the D N A inside a condensed structure. Methylation pulls the elements into the major groove. In both cases the recognition step never happens. The protein does not get to the helix at all.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>它们挡在同一步上</b>。<b>两者都没有改动结合元件的任何一个碱基，所以它们改的都不是「蛋白认得出什么」，而是「蛋白够得着什么」。</b><b>染色质把 DNA 藏进致密结构里；甲基化把元件缩进大沟里。</b>⚠ <b>两种情形下，「识别」这一步根本没有发生过——蛋白压根没够到双螺旋。</b><b>这就是把它们放在同一道关卡上的理由。</b>',
   en:'“Because they block at the same step. Neither of them changes a base of the binding element, so neither can be changing what the protein recognises. What they change is what a protein can physically reach. Packing hides the DNA inside a condensed structure, and methylation shifts the duplex towards Z-DNA so the elements are pulled into the major groove. In both cases the recognition step never happens, because the protein never gets to the helix.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Why does the yeast two-hybrid system work at all?',
   ez:'“Because an activator has two separable domains. The D N A binding domain decides which site is recognised. The activation domain does the activating. Normally one protein carries both. But they can be split onto two proteins. Fuse one protein of interest to the binding domain. Fuse the other to the activation domain. If the two interact the domains are brought together. Then the reporter gene downstream is switched on.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>激活因子的两个结构域是可以拆开的两块</b>：<b>DNA 结合域决定认哪个位点，转录激活域负责激活；平时它们长在同一个蛋白上，但可以被分到两个蛋白上去。</b><b>把一个目标蛋白融合到 DNA 结合域上，另一个融合到转录激活域上——两者一旦相互作用，两个结构域就被拉到一起，下游的报告基因随之打开。</b><b>酵母三杂交里把两个融合蛋白牵到一起的是一条能同时结合两者的 RNA，于是报告的就是 RNA 与蛋白质的相互作用。</b>',
   en:'“Because an activator has two separable domains. The DNA-binding domain decides which site is recognised, and the activation domain does the activating. Normally one protein carries both, but they can be split across two proteins. Fuse one protein of interest to the binding domain and the other to the activation domain, and if the two interact the domains are brought together and the downstream reporter gene is switched on. In the three-hybrid version an RNA able to bind both fusions does the bringing together, so the reporter reports an RNA and protein interaction instead.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Why does a deacetylase complex not silence the whole genome?',
   ez:'“Because it only works once it has been recruited. The complex has no site preference of its own. Something else has to bring it to a promoter. So which genes fall silent is decided by the recruiter. At cell cycle promoters the recruiter is Rb. Rb is a tumour suppressor bound to E two F there. With E two F bound it brings H D A C one across. Then that promoter alone is deacetylated and condensed.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>它必须先被募集到某一个启动子上才起作用</b>：<b>这个复合体本身没有位点偏好，得由别的东西把它带过去——所以「哪些基因被沉默」是由负责募集的那个蛋白决定的。</b><b>在细胞周期基因这里，负责募集的是抑癌蛋白 Rb：它与 E2F 类激活因子结合在这些基因的启动子上，结合了 E2F 的 Rb 再把 HDAC1 拉过来，使该启动子区特异性去乙酰化、染色质浓缩。</b>',
   en:'“Because it only works once it has been recruited. The complex has no site preference of its own, so something else has to bring it to a promoter, and which genes fall silent is decided by whatever does the recruiting. Yeast Rpd3 works with the co-repressor Sin3. Human HDAC1 at cell-cycle promoters is brought there by the retinoblastoma protein, a tumour suppressor bound to E2F, and only that promoter region is then deacetylated and condensed.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Why is five-methylcytosine called a mutagen as well as a switch?',
   ez:'“Because the same modification does two different things. As a switch it lowers transcription reversibly. Remove the methyl and the gene comes back. But five methyl cytosine also deaminates into thymine. Thymine is not easily recognised by the repair system. So the site takes a heritable C to T transition. That part is permanent and cannot be undone. Over a third of human transition diseases start from this.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>同一种修饰在做两件不同的事</b>。<b>作为开关，它可逆地降低转录——把甲基去掉，基因就回来了。</b><b>但 5-mC 还会脱氨生成胸腺嘧啶，而 T 不易被修复系统识别和矫正，于是这个位点留下一个可遗传的 C→T 转换——这一部分是永久的，撤不回来。</b><b>人体中由碱基转换引起的遗传病，三分之一以上源自 CpG 中胞嘧啶的甲基化。</b>',
   en:'“Because the same modification does two different things. As a switch it lowers transcription reversibly, and removing the methyl brings the gene back. But five-methylcytosine also deaminates into thymine, and thymine is not easily recognised and corrected by the repair system, so the site takes a heritable C to T transition which cannot be undone. More than a third of human genetic diseases caused by base transitions start from a methylated cytosine in CpG, and codon two hundred and seventy-three of p53 is the standard example.”'}
 ]},

 {g:'⚠ 陷阱', gn:'说错了听起来还挺对的地方。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'（陷阱）把「转录活性」和「有功能的 mRNA」混着说',
   ez:'“They are two different things. Mutating AATAAA into AAGAAA is the clean case. The transcriptional activity of the gene is unchanged. The processing of the transcript is blocked. So the transcript is still made. No functional messenger R N A comes out of it. Transcription and processing fail separately.”',
   ezcn:'⚠ <b>两件事。</b><b>把 AATAAA 点突变成 AAGAAA 是最干净的例子：基因的转录活性照旧保持，而 mRNA 的加工被阻断——转录产物照样做出来，却产生不了有功能的 mRNA。</b><b>转录和加工是各自会坏的两步。</b>',
   en:'“They are two different things, and AATAAA is the clean case. A point mutation turning AATAAA into AAGAAA leaves the transcriptional activity of the gene unchanged while blocking the processing of the transcript. The transcript is still made, and no functional messenger RNA comes out of it. Transcription and processing are two steps that fail separately.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）说「甲基化把序列改掉了」',
   ez:'“It does not change the sequence while it acts. It adds a methyl group to a base. The base pairing and the sequence stay as they were. What changes is the shape of the helix. The elements get pulled into the major groove out of reach. Only later, if the methylated cytosine deaminates, does the sequence change. That is a separate event and it is permanent.”',
   ezcn:'⚠ <b>甲基化在起作用的时候并没有改序列</b>：它只是在碱基上加了一个甲基，配对和序列都照旧，<b>变的是双螺旋的形状——元件被缩进大沟里够不着</b>。<b>只有在后来那个甲基胞嘧啶脱氨的时候，序列才真的被改掉——那是另一件事，而且是永久的。</b>',
   en:'“Methylation does not change the sequence while it acts. It adds a methyl group to a base, and the base pairing and the sequence stay as they were. What changes is the shape of the helix, so the elements are pulled into the major groove out of reach. Only later, if that methylated cytosine deaminates into thymine, does the sequence itself change. That is a separate event, and a permanent one.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）说「亮氨酸拉链结合 DNA」',
   ez:'“The zipper does not bind D N A. It makes the dimer. Every seventh leucine lies on the same face of the helix. Those faces zip two helices together. What binds D N A is the basic region. That is twenty to thirty residues at the amino end. And without dimerisation its affinity drops markedly. So the binding domain is really the basic region plus the zipper.”',
   ezcn:'⚠ <b>亮氨酸拉链区本身并不结合 DNA，它负责二聚</b>：每第 7 个亮氨酸出现在螺旋的同一方向，两条螺旋靠这一侧拉成二聚体。<b>真正结合 DNA 的是肽链氨基端 20～30 个富含碱性氨基酸的结构域；而若不形成二聚体，这个碱性区对 DNA 的亲和力明显降低。</b><b>所以这里的「DNA 结合结构域」实际是碱性区与拉链区合起来的整体。</b>',
   en:'“The leucine zipper does not bind DNA. It makes the dimer. Every seventh leucine lies on the same face of the helix, and those faces zip two helices together. What binds DNA is the basic region, twenty to thirty residues at the amino end, and without dimerisation its affinity for DNA drops markedly. So the DNA-binding domain here is really the basic region and the zipper taken together.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）以为顺式和反式说的是「在哪里」',
   ez:'“The names describe how each acts, not where it sits. A cis element acts on the D N A molecule it lies on. That is why deleting it affects only that copy of the gene. A trans factor is a diffusible product. It is made somewhere and then acts elsewhere. That is why it can act on both copies and on other genes.”',
   ezcn:'⚠ <b>命名的依据是「怎么起作用」，不是「在哪里」。</b><b>顺式元件作用在自己所在的那条 DNA 分子上——所以把它删掉，只影响这一份拷贝上的那个基因。</b><b>反式因子是可以扩散的产物：在某处被做出来，然后跑到别处去起作用——所以它能同时作用于两份拷贝，也能作用于别的基因。</b>',
   en:'“The names describe how each one acts, not where it sits. A cis element acts on the DNA molecule it lies on, which is why deleting it affects only that copy of the gene. A trans factor is a diffusible product, made somewhere and then acting elsewhere, which is why it can act on both copies and on other genes as well.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（陷阱）把组蛋白甲基化一律当成「关」',
   ez:'“Methylation of a histone tail is not one signal. The meaning depends on the residue and the number of groups. H three K nine me three does silence. So does H three K twenty seven me three. But H three K four me three marks transcription start sites. And H three K thirty six me three covers the transcribed region. Those two are marks of an active region.”',
   ezcn:'⚠ <b>组蛋白甲基化不是一个信号。</b><b>含义取决于加在哪个残基上、加了几个：H3K9me3 和 H3K27me3 确实是沉默，但 H3K4me3 富集在转录起始位点、H3K36me3 遍布整个转录区，这两个都是转录活性区的标记。</b>',
   en:'“Methylation of a histone tail is not one signal. What it means depends on which residue of which histone carries it, and on how many groups there are. H3K9me3 and H3K27me3 do silence. But H3K4me3 is enriched at transcription start sites and H3K36me3 runs across the whole transcribed region, and both of those are read as marks of an actively transcribed region.”'}
 ]},

 {g:'相邻考点', gn:'从这道题最容易走到哪儿。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'（走向 mb-ko）How would you test whether a sequence is really an enhancer?',
   ez:'“You use a reporter that cannot switch itself on. Build a construct with lacZ and a weak basal promoter. That promoter alone cannot drive the reporter. Integrate it into the genome at random. The reporter is then expressed only near an enhancer. So expression itself reports the enhancer. And it reports when and where that enhancer acts. Gene trapping uses the same trick for genes.”',
   ezcn:'<b>用一个自己开不起来的报告基因。</b><b>做一个带 lacZ 和一个本身不足以启动它的基本启动子的转化载体，随机整合进基因组——只有当插入位点附近有增强子时 lacZ 才表达。</b><b>于是「表达」这件事本身就报告了那里有增强子，而且报告出它在什么时间、什么部位起作用。</b>⚠ <b>mb-ko 上的基因捕获用的是同一个把戏，只是报告的对象换成了基因。</b>',
   en:'“With a reporter that cannot switch itself on. Build a transformation vector carrying lacZ together with a basal promoter too weak to drive it, and integrate it into the genome at random. The reporter is then expressed only where the insertion has landed near an enhancer, so expression itself reports the enhancer. And it reports at what time and in what part of the organism that enhancer acts. Gene trapping uses the same trick, with a promoterless reporter, to report genes instead.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（走向 12）How does this compare with the lac operon?',
   ez:'“The eukaryotic version is the same idea with more layers. In both cases a protein binds a D N A element. In both cases that decides whether transcription happens. But a prokaryote has no chromatin gate. There is no nucleosome to open first. And a prokaryotic operon is polycistronic. One promoter serves several genes. A eukaryotic gene has its own promoter. So each one is regulated on its own.”',
   ezcn:'<b>真核版本是同一个想法，只是多了几层。</b><b>两边都是「蛋白结合到一段 DNA 元件上，由此决定转不转录」。</b><b>但原核没有染色质这一道关卡——没有核小体要先打开；而且原核操纵子是多顺反子的，一个启动子管好几个基因，真核基因各有各的启动子，所以每个都单独被调控。</b>',
   en:'“The eukaryotic version is the same idea with more layers on top. In both cases a protein binds a DNA element, and in both cases that decides whether transcription happens. But a prokaryote has no chromatin gate. There is no nucleosome to open first, and no DNA methylation standing between the factor and the helix. A prokaryotic operon is also polycistronic, so one promoter serves several genes, whereas a eukaryotic gene has its own promoter and is regulated on its own.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（走向 16）Where else does the major groove matter?',
   ez:'“It matters wherever a protein has to read the sequence. The major groove is where the bases can be told apart. Helix turn helix puts its third helix there. Zinc fingers line their helices up along it. And methylation blocks by pulling elements into it. So reading and blocking happen in the same place. That is why a conformational change is enough to stop recognition.”',
   ezcn:'<b>凡是蛋白必须「读」序列的地方，大沟都要紧</b>：<b>大沟是碱基能被分辨出来的那一面。</b><b>HTH 把第三个螺旋放进大沟，锌指把各自的螺旋几乎连成一线排在大沟里；而甲基化正是靠把元件缩进大沟里来阻断的。</b>⚠ <b>读和挡发生在同一个地方——所以只要构象一变，识别就停了，不必改动任何一个碱基。</b>',
   en:'“Wherever a protein has to read the sequence. The major groove is the face on which the bases can be told apart, so that is where recognition happens. The homeodomain puts its third helix there, and repeated zinc fingers line their helices up along it. And methylation blocks transcription precisely by pulling the binding elements down into that groove. Reading and blocking happen in the same place, which is why a change of conformation alone is enough to stop recognition without altering a single base.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'（走向下一张卡）What layers of regulation come after transcription?',
   ez:'“Several, and R N A modification is one of them. m six A is the commonest one on messenger R N A. It needs the same three parts as a histone mark. A writer complex built around METTL three adds it. Erasers such as F T O remove it. Readers bind it through a Y T H domain. It changes splicing and export and stability and translation. So a gene can be turned down with its chromatin untouched.”',
   ezcn:'<b>好几层，RNA 修饰是其中之一。</b><b>m⁶A 是 mRNA 上较常见的一种，它跟组蛋白标记需要同样的三件组：以 METTL3 为核心的写入复合物、FTO 和 ALKBH5 这样的擦除酶、通过 YTH 结构域读取它的蛋白。</b><b>它影响剪接、核输出、稳定性和翻译——所以一个基因可以在染色质完全没被碰过的情况下被调低。</b>',
   en:'“Several, and chemical modification of RNA is one of them. N6-methyladenosine, m6A, is the commonest one on messenger RNA, found at sites in nearly seven thousand messenger RNAs in mouse and human cells. It needs the same three parts as a histone mark. There is a writer, the methyltransferase complex built around METTL3. There are erasers such as FTO and ALKBH5. And there are readers that bind it through a YTH domain. It works by changing RNA secondary structure, and it affects splicing, nuclear export, stability and translation, so a gene can be turned down with neither its DNA nor its chromatin touched.”'}
 ]},

 {g:'桥回主场', gn:'把话拉回你真正做的事。', items:[
  {r:'高', q:'Does any of this matter for your own work?',
   ez:'“It matters as the thing I design out. All of this is a cell controlling its own genes. In my work I put a gene under a promoter I choose. Then I hold the conditions constant. The point is to stop regulation being a variable. Only then does a difference between variants mean the protein. Otherwise it could just mean a different expression level. So the same machinery is the subject here and a confounder there.”',
   ezcn:'<b>它对我而言是「要被设计掉」的那个东西。</b><b>这一整套说的是细胞怎么调控自己的基因；而我的工作里，我把基因放在自己选的启动子下面、把条件固定住，目的就是让调控不再是变量。</b>⚠ <b>只有这样，变体之间的差别才能被读成「蛋白不一样」，否则它同样可能只是「表达量不一样」。</b><b>同一套机制，在这里是研究对象，在我那里是要排除掉的干扰。</b>',
   en:'“It matters as the thing I design out. All of this is a cell controlling its own genes. In my work I put a gene under a promoter I choose and hold the conditions constant, precisely so that regulation stops being a variable. Only then can a difference between variants be read as a difference in the protein rather than a difference in expression level. So the same machinery is the subject here and a confounder there.”'},

  {r:'中', q:'Why does a display library use a strong constitutive promoter?',
   ez:'“The selection has to compare proteins and not promoters. A regulated promoter responds to the state of each cell. Then two cells could differ by state alone. And the selection would pick the state and not the variant. A strong constitutive promoter holds that constant. So what varies between cells is the coding sequence. That is the only thing the selection should be reading.”',
   ezcn:'因为<b>筛选要比较的是蛋白，不是启动子</b>。<b>一个受调控的启动子会对每个细胞各自的状态作出反应，那么两个细胞之间可能只是状态不同——筛选挑中的就会是状态，而不是变体。</b><b>用一个强的组成型启动子把这一项固定住，细胞之间唯一还在变的就是编码序列，而那正是筛选应该读的唯一一件事。</b>',
   en:'“Because the selection has to compare proteins, not promoters. A regulated promoter responds to the state of each individual cell, so two cells could differ by state alone and the selection would be picking the state rather than the variant. A strong constitutive promoter holds that term constant, so the only thing still varying between cells is the coding sequence, and that is the only thing the selection should be reading.”'}
 ]},
 {g:'⚠ 书外 · 甲基化的另一面：它同时在毁掉这个位点', gn:'1 条，出自《现代分子生物学》第五版 <b>p.066</b>。<b>接在 CpG 岛那一格后面</b>——卡上讲的是甲基化关掉转录，这一条讲的是同一个甲基化让这个 C 自己变成 T。', items:[
{r:'中', q:'Why is a methylated CpG the most mutable site in the human genome?',
    ez:'“A methylated cytosine loses its amino group on its own. That turns it into thymine. No replication error is needed. No damaging agent is needed either. A CpG is a C followed by a G on one strand. Most of those cytosines are methylated. So each one is a C that turns itself into a T. Repeat that over a whole genome. The result shows up in the mutation catalogue. A single nucleotide polymorphism is a change at one base. A transition swaps a purine for a purine. It also covers a pyrimidine for a pyrimidine. A transversion swaps a purine for a pyrimidine. Transitions are about two thirds of all such polymorphisms. The methylated CpG is why.”',
    ezcn:'<b>CpG 二核苷酸（同一条链上一个 C 紧跟着一个 G）上的胞嘧啶残基，是人类基因组中最易发生突变的位点。</b>⚠ <b>因为这些胞嘧啶大多数是甲基化的，而甲基化的胞嘧啶会<b>自发地脱去氨基变成胸腺嘧啶</b>——不需要复制出错，也不需要任何损伤因子。一个甲基化的 CpG 就是一个会自己变成 T 的 C。</b><b>把这件事在整个基因组上重复一遍，就得到了突变目录里的那个偏倚：<b>SNP（单核苷酸多态性）</b>位点上的变化分两类——<b>转换（transition）</b>是嘌呤换嘌呤、嘧啶换嘧啶，<b>颠换（transversion）</b>是嘌呤换嘧啶或反过来；而<b>转换约占 SNP 总量的三分之二</b>。</b>⚠ <b>所以一个位点上可能发生的替换远非等概率，整个目录被其中一类改变主导着。</b>',
 en:'“The cytosine of a CpG dinucleotide, meaning a C followed immediately by a G on the same strand, is the most mutable site in the human genome. The reason is that most of those cytosines are methylated, and a methylated cytosine spontaneously loses its amino group and becomes thymine. No replication error is needed and no damaging agent is needed. A methylated CpG is simply a C that turns itself into a T. Repeat that across a whole genome and it shows up in the catalogue of variation. A single nucleotide polymorphism is a variation caused by the mutation of one nucleotide. The change at such a site is either a transition or a transversion. A transition is a purine for another purine, or a pyrimidine for another pyrimidine. A transversion is a purine for a pyrimidine, or the reverse. Transitions make up about two thirds of all single nucleotide polymorphisms. So the substitutions possible at a site are nowhere near equally likely, and the whole catalogue is dominated by one class of change, because of the methylated CpG.”',
 cn:'<b>p.066</b>。⚠ <b>这条是这张卡 CpG 岛那一格的反面</b>：卡上说的是甲基化<b>关掉转录</b>，这里说的是同一个甲基化<b>同时在毁掉这个位点</b>。<b>SNP 的其余内容（分类与用途）</b>：按位置分三类——<b>cSNP</b> 在编码区、<b>pSNP</b> 在调控区、<b>rSNP</b> 在基因间随机非编码区；编码区变异率只有周围序列的 1/5，所以 <b>cSNP 总量显著少于另两类——最可能有影响的位点恰好最难找到</b>。<b>同义 cSNP</b> 不改变氨基酸序列，<b>非同义 cSNP</b> 改变；<b>pSNP</b> 改变的是表达量。⚠ <b>非同义 cSNP 和 pSNP 是疾病上真正有分量的两类：一类改变蛋白质是什么，另一类改变蛋白质有多少。</b>人类基因组里每 300～1 000 bp 就有一个 SNP，一个人身上有 300 万～1 000 万个。'},
 ]}
]
});
